(window.APUSH_TOPICS=window.APUSH_TOPICS||{})[4]=[{"id": "p4-001", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Samuel Slater and the First Spinning Mill (1790)", "topic_zh": "塞缪尔·斯莱特与第一座纺纱厂", "year": 1790, "year_text": "1790", "who": ["Samuel Slater", "Richard Arkwright", "Moses Brown"], "who_zh": ["塞缪尔·斯莱特", "理查德·阿克赖特", "摩西·布朗"], "what_en": "Samuel Slater, described as the most important emigre mechanic, came to America in 1789 after working for Richard Arkwright, inventor of the most advanced British machinery for spinning cotton. A year later, Slater reproduced Arkwright's innovations in merchant Moses Brown's cotton mill in Providence, Rhode Island.", "what_zh": "被称为最重要的移民技工的塞缪尔·斯莱特，1789 年在为阿克赖特（最先进的英国纺纱机械发明者）工作后来到美国。一年后（1790 年），他在罗德岛普罗维登斯商人摩西·布朗的棉纺厂中复制了阿克赖特的创新。", "cause_en": "The British government prohibited the export of textile machinery and the emigration of mechanics, but lured by higher wages, thousands of British mechanics disguised themselves as laborers and sailed to the United States; by 1812 at least three hundred worked in the Philadelphia area alone.", "cause_zh": "英国政府禁止纺织机械出口和技工移民，但受高工资吸引，数千英国技工乔装成劳工漂洋过海；到 1812 年，仅费城地区就有至少三百名英国技工。", "sig_en": "Slater's mill launched American textile manufacturing; soon, waterways from Massachusetts to Delaware were lined with industrial villages and textile mills as large as 150 feet long and four stories high.", "sig_zh": "斯莱特的纺纱厂开启了美国纺织制造业；不久，从马萨诸塞到特拉华的河道两岸就布满了工业村庄和长达 150 英尺、四层楼高的纺纱厂。", "exp_en": "Slater pirated British spinning technology for an American mill, making the United States a textile producer instead of just a cotton supplier.", "exp_zh": "斯莱特把英国纺纱技术“盗版”到美国建厂，使美国从棉花原料供应国变成了纺织品生产国。", "page": 287}, {"id": "p4-002", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Francis Cabot Lowell, the Boston Manufacturing Company, and the Waltham-Lowell System", "topic_zh": "弗朗西斯·卡博特·洛厄尔、波士顿制造公司与沃尔瑟姆-洛厄尔体系", "year": 1814, "year_text": "1814", "who": ["Francis Cabot Lowell", "Paul Moody", "Nathan Appleton", "Patrick Tracy Jackson"], "who_zh": ["弗朗西斯·卡博特·洛厄尔", "保罗·穆迪", "内森·阿普尔顿", "帕特里克·特雷西·杰克逊"], "what_en": "In 1811, wealthy Boston merchant Francis Cabot Lowell toured British textile mills, secretly making detailed drawings of their power machinery; American mechanic Paul Moody copied and improved the machines. In 1814, Lowell joined merchants Nathan Appleton and Patrick Tracy Jackson to form the Boston Manufacturing Company, raised $400,000, and built a textile plant in Waltham, Massachusetts - the first American factory to perform all clothmaking operations under one roof. In the 1820s the company recruited thousands of young farm women, housing them in boardinghouses with curfews, alcohol bans, and required church attendance; by the early 1830s more than 40,000 New England women worked in textile mills.", "what_zh": "1811 年，波士顿富商弗朗西斯·卡博特·洛厄尔参观英国纺织厂，秘密绘制了动力机械的详细图纸；美国技工保罗·穆迪复制并改进了这些机器。1814 年，洛厄尔与商人内森·阿普尔顿、帕特里克·特雷西·杰克逊组建波士顿制造公司，筹资 40 万美元，在马萨诸塞州沃尔瑟姆建厂——美国第一家把全部织布工序集中在一栋屋顶下的工厂。1820 年代公司招募数千农家少女，让她们住宿舍、实行宵禁、禁酒、强制上教堂；到 1830 年代初，新英格兰已有 4 万多名女性在纺织厂做工。", "cause_en": "British producers easily undersold American competitors thanks to cheap transatlantic shipping, low interest rates, and cheap labor, so American entrepreneurs combined improved technology, a cheaper female labor force, and protective tariffs (1816, 1824, 1828).", "cause_zh": "英国厂商凭借廉价的跨大西洋海运、低利率和廉价劳动力轻易压低价格，因此美国企业家把改进的技术、更便宜的女性劳动力和保护性关税（1816、1824、1828 年）结合起来竞争。", "sig_en": "The Waltham plant's power looms operated at higher speeds than British looms with fewer workers, and the Waltham-Lowell System gave young farm women wages greater than housework could provide and a measure of independence.", "sig_zh": "沃尔瑟姆厂的动力织机比英国织机转速更快、用工更少；沃尔瑟姆-洛厄尔体系让农家少女获得高于家务劳动的工资和更大的独立性。", "exp_en": "Lowell's company integrated spinning and weaving under one roof and pioneered the factory employment of young women, setting the model for American textile industrialization.", "exp_zh": "洛厄尔的公司把纺纱织布集中于一厂，并首创雇佣年轻女工的工厂模式，成为美国纺织工业化的样板。", "page": 287, "src": {"text": "more than could be obtained by the hitherto ordinary occupation of housework", "attr": "an observer quoted in the text"}}, {"id": "p4-003", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Eli Whitney: the Cotton Gin (1793) and Interchangeable Parts", "topic_zh": "伊莱·惠特尼：轧棉机与可互换零件", "year": 1793, "year_text": "1793", "who": ["Eli Whitney", "John H. Hall"], "who_zh": ["伊莱·惠特尼", "约翰·H·霍尔"], "what_en": "In 1793, using his expertise in making hatpins, Eli Whitney built a simple machine that separated the seeds in a cotton boll from the delicate fibers, work previously done slowly by hand. Although he patented his cotton engine (gin), other manufacturers improved on his design and captured the market. In 1798 he turned to manufacturing military weapons and designed machine tools that could rapidly produce interchangeable musket parts, bringing him wealth and fame.", "what_zh": "1793 年，惠特尼运用制作帽针的技术，造出了一台把棉籽从棉纤维中分离的简单机器（此前全靠手工慢速完成）。他虽为这台“轧棉机”申请了专利，但其他厂商改进设计后抢走了市场。1798 年他转向军火制造，设计出能快速生产可互换滑膛枪零件的机床，从此名利双收。", "cause_en": "Whitney, the son of a middling New England farm family who won admission to Yale, worked as a tutor on a Georgia cotton plantation and aspired to wealth and status.", "cause_zh": "出身新英格兰普通农家的惠特尼考入耶鲁后在佐治亚棉花种植园当家庭教师，一心追求财富与地位。", "sig_en": "The cotton gin mechanized cotton processing, and Whitney's interchangeable parts pioneered the American machine-tool industry and standardized mass production.", "sig_zh": "轧棉机使棉花加工机械化；惠特尼的可互换零件开创了美国机床工业和标准化大批量生产。", "exp_en": "Whitney's two inventions mechanized both Southern agriculture and Northern manufacturing, anchoring the Industrial Revolution's technology.", "exp_zh": "惠特尼的两项发明分别使南方农业和北方制造业机械化，成为工业革命技术的支柱。", "page": 290, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2820", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.290"}}, {"id": "p4-004", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Division of Labor and the Factory", "topic_zh": "劳动分工与工厂", "year": null, "year_text": "1820s-1830s", "who": ["Lynn shoemakers", "Cincinnati pork packers"], "who_zh": ["林恩制鞋商", "辛辛那提肉类加工商"], "what_en": "During the 1820s and 1830s, merchants in Lynn, Massachusetts, destroyed independent shoemakers' businesses by introducing an outwork system and a division of labor: journeymen cut leather into soles and uppers in large shops, rural women binders sewed in fabric linings, and other journeymen attached uppers to soles. In the 1830s, Cincinnati merchants built huge slaughterhouses where a division of labor moved hog carcasses along a disassembly line - one worker split the animals, another removed organs, others trimmed carcasses - processing sixty hogs an hour.", "what_zh": "1820 至 1830 年代，马萨诸塞州林恩的商人引入外包制和劳动分工，摧毁了独立鞋匠的生意：熟练工在大作坊里把皮革裁成鞋底鞋面，乡下女工缝制内衬，另一些熟练工把鞋面钉到鞋底上。1830 年代，辛辛那提商人建造大型屠宰场，用劳动分工让猪胴体沿“拆解线”移动——一人开膛、一人取内脏、余人切块，每小时处理 60 头猪。", "cause_en": "Manufacturers sought higher output and lower prices by reorganizing work, turning independent artisans into semiskilled wage laborers.", "cause_zh": "制造商通过重组生产流程追求更高产量和更低价格，把独立工匠变成了半熟练雇佣工人。", "sig_en": "The more efficient system cut the price of shoes and boots even as it turned employers into powerful shoe bosses and eroded workers' wages and independence; by the 1840s Cincinnati was known as Porkopolis.", "sig_zh": "更高效的体系压低了鞋靴价格，但雇主变成了强势的“鞋老板”，工人的工资和独立性被侵蚀；到 1840 年代辛辛那提被称为“猪肉城”。", "exp_en": "Division of labor made mass production possible but converted self-employed artisans into supervised wage earners.", "exp_zh": "劳动分工使大批量生产成为可能，但也把自雇工匠变成了受监督的雇佣工人。", "page": 286, "src": {"text": "We took out our watches and counted thirty-five seconds, from the moment when one hog touched the table until the next occupied its place.", "attr": "Frederick Law Olmsted, landscape architect and journalist"}}, {"id": "p4-005", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Machine Tools and the Sellars Family", "topic_zh": "机床与塞拉斯家族", "year": null, "year_text": "1820s-1860", "who": ["the Sellars family", "Samuel Sellars Jr.", "John Sellars"], "who_zh": ["塞拉斯家族", "小塞缪尔·塞拉斯", "约翰·塞拉斯"], "what_en": "American craftsmen pioneered machine tools - machines that made parts for other machines. In the Philadelphia region the Sellars family produced leading inventors: Samuel Sellars Jr. invented a machine for twisting worsted woolen yarn; his son John improved waterwheels and built a machine to weave wire sieves; later generations ran machine shops turning out fire hoses, papermaking equipment, and eventually locomotives. In 1824 the Sellars and other mechanics founded Philadelphia's Franklin Institute to publish a journal, teach chemistry, mathematics, and mechanical design, and exhibit new products. Between 1820 and 1860, U.S. patents rose from two hundred to four thousand a year.", "what_zh": "美国工匠率先发展了机床——制造其他机器零件的机器。费城地区的塞拉斯家族涌现出一批重要发明家：小塞缪尔·塞拉斯发明了加捻精纺毛纱的机器；其子约翰改进水车并制造了织金属筛网的机器；后代经营的机械作坊生产消防水带、造纸设备乃至机车。1824 年塞拉斯等人创办费城富兰克林学院，出版刊物、教授化学数学机械设计、展出新产品。1820 至 1860 年，美国专利年授权量从 200 件增至 4000 件。", "cause_en": "By the 1820s, American-born artisans had replaced British immigrants at the cutting edge of technological innovation, though few had formal education.", "cause_zh": "到 1820 年代，土生美国工匠取代英国移民站到了技术创新的最前沿，尽管他们大多没受过正规教育。", "sig_en": "Machine tools enabled the mass production of precisely made, standardized parts, letting American jennies and looms run at higher speeds than British equipment and making the U.S. competitive in world manufacturing.", "sig_zh": "机床使精密标准化零件的大批量生产成为可能，美国纺纱机织布机转速超过英国设备，美国制造业开始具备全球竞争力。", "exp_en": "Machine tools and technical institutes like the Franklin Institute spread mechanical know-how and powered the maturation of American manufacturing.", "exp_zh": "机床和富兰克林学院这类技术机构传播了机械知识，推动美国制造业走向成熟。", "page": 290, "src": {"text": "with machinery applied to almost every process . . . all reduced to an almost perfect system of manufacture", "attr": "British observers"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2820", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.290"}}, {"id": "p4-006", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Artisan Republicanism and the Labor Theory of Value", "topic_zh": "工匠共和主义与劳动价值论", "year": null, "year_text": "1830s", "who": ["craft workers", "journeymen shoemakers"], "who_zh": ["手工艺工人", "熟练鞋匠"], "what_en": "After the Revolution, many craft workers espoused artisan republicanism, an ideology of production based on liberty and equality: they saw themselves as small-scale producers, equal to one another and free to work for themselves. As factories spread, wageworkers rejected the terms master and servant, calling employers by the Dutch word boss. Union leaders expanded artisan republicanism to wageworkers and advanced a labor theory of value: the price of goods should reflect the labor required to make them, and the income from sales should go primarily to the producers, not to factory owners, middlemen, or storekeepers.", "what_zh": "革命后，许多手工艺工人信奉工匠共和主义——一种以自由平等为基础的生产意识形态：他们把自己看作彼此平等、为自己劳动的小生产者。随着工厂蔓延，雇佣工人摒弃“主人/仆人”称谓，用荷兰语 boss 称呼雇主。工会领袖把工匠共和主义扩展到雇佣工人，并提出劳动价值论：商品价格应反映制造它所需的劳动，销售收入应主要归生产者，而非厂主、中间商或店主。", "cause_en": "The spread of the outwork and factory systems turned independent artisans into supervised wage earners with meager wages and little job security; labor had become a commodity to be bought and sold.", "cause_zh": "外包制和工厂制的蔓延把独立工匠变成了受监督、工资微薄、缺乏保障的雇佣工人；劳动力成了可买卖的商品。", "sig_en": "Artisan republicanism and the labor theory of value gave the 1830s labor movement its ideology, fueling union organizing such as the National Trades Union of 1834 and demands that producers receive a fair share of profits.", "sig_zh": "工匠共和主义和劳动价值论为 1830 年代劳工运动提供了意识形态，推动了 1834 年全国工会等组织和生产者分享利润的诉求。", "why_term": "labor theory of value", "why_term_q": "教材强调的、主张产品收入应主要归生产者的分配理论（关键词）是 ______。", "exp_en": "Workers adapted artisan republicanism to industrial wage labor, insisting that value comes from labor and belongs to laborers.", "exp_zh": "工人把工匠共和主义改造为适应工业雇佣劳动的理论，坚持价值来自劳动、应归于劳动者。", "page": 291, "src": {"text": "The capitalist has no other interest in us, than to get as much labor out of us as possible. We are hired men, and hired men, like hired horses, have no souls.", "attr": "journeymen shoemakers' mutual benefit societies"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2823", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.291"}}, {"id": "p4-007", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Commonwealth v. Hunt (1842)", "topic_zh": "共和联邦诉亨特案", "year": 1842, "year_text": "1842", "who": ["Lemuel Shaw"], "who_zh": ["莱缪尔·肖"], "what_en": "In Commonwealth v. Hunt (1842), Chief Justice Lemuel Shaw of the Massachusetts Supreme Judicial Court overturned common-law precedents and upheld the right of workers to form unions and call strikes to enforce closed-shop agreements that limited employment to union members.", "what_zh": "1842 年共和联邦诉亨特案中，马萨诸塞州最高司法法院首席法官莱缪尔·肖推翻普通法先例，确认工人有权组建工会并发起罢工，以执行只雇佣工会成员的闭厂协议。", "cause_en": "English and American common law branded unions as illegal combinations; courts convicted unions of conspiring to raise wages - a Philadelphia judge called them a government unto themselves and the New York Supreme Court upheld a conspiracy verdict in 1835.", "cause_zh": "英美普通法把工会定为非法“结社”；法院以“串谋涨薪”定罪工会——费城法官称工会是“国中之国”，1835 年纽约最高法院也维持了串谋有罪判决。", "sig_en": "The decision was the first major legal legitimation of American trade unions, though many judges continued to resist unions by issuing injunctions forbidding strikes.", "sig_zh": "该判决是美国工会获得的第一次重大法律认可，但许多法官仍继续用禁令阻止罢工。", "exp_en": "Commonwealth v. Hunt removed the conspiracy-law weapon against unions and legalized collective bargaining by workers.", "exp_zh": "亨特案解除了针对工会的串谋法武器，使工人集体谈判合法化。", "page": 292, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2826", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.292"}}, {"id": "p4-008", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The Erie Canal (1817-1825)", "topic_zh": "伊利运河", "year": 1825, "year_text": "1817-1825 (completed 1825)", "who": ["De Witt Clinton", "New York legislature"], "who_zh": ["德威特·克林顿", "纽约州议会"], "what_en": "In 1817 the New York legislature financed the Erie Canal, a 364-mile waterway connecting the Hudson River and Lake Erie. Backed by New York City merchants and Governor De Witt Clinton, who proposed financing it from tax revenues, tolls, and bond sales to foreign investors, workers - many of them Irish immigrants - dug out millions of cubic yards of soil for the locks. The first great engineering project in American history, it was completed in 1825: a 40-foot-wide ribbon of water from Buffalo to Albany, where it joined the Hudson for the 150-mile trip to New York City.", "what_zh": "1817 年纽约州议会出资修建伊利运河，一条连接哈德逊河与伊利湖的 364 英里水道。在纽约市商人和州长德威特·克林顿（主张用税收、通行费和向外国投资者售债融资）的支持下，大批工人（多为爱尔兰移民）挖出数百万立方码土方修建船闸。这项美国历史上第一个大型工程于 1825 年完工：一条 40 英尺宽的水带从布法罗通到奥尔巴尼，再经哈德逊河 150 英里直抵纽约市。", "cause_en": "Overland travel was slow and expensive, and the longest previous American canal was only 28 miles; midwestern settlers needed a cheap water route linking the Great Lakes region to eastern markets.", "cause_zh": "陆路运输又慢又贵，此前美国最长的运河仅 28 英里；中西部定居者需要一条连接五大湖地区与东部市场的廉价水路。", "sig_en": "The canal was an instant economic success - its first 75-mile section opened in 1819 quickly repaid its construction cost; it brought prosperity to farmers of central and western New York and the Great Lakes region, prompted a national canal boom, and forged the Northeast-Midwest commercial bond at the heart of the Market Revolution.", "sig_zh": "运河即刻取得经济成功——1819 年通车的第一段 75 英里很快收回造价；它使纽约中西部和五大湖地区的农民繁荣起来，引发全国运河热，并铸就了市场革命核心的东北—中西部商业纽带。", "exp_en": "The Erie Canal shrank distance between the Atlantic and the Great Lakes, turning the Midwest into a commercial partner of the Northeast.", "exp_zh": "伊利运河拉近了大西洋与五大湖的距离，使中西部成为东北的商业伙伴。", "page": 293}, {"id": "p4-009", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Gibbons v. Ogden (1824)", "topic_zh": "吉本斯诉奥格登案", "year": 1824, "year_text": "1824", "who": ["John Marshall", "U.S. Supreme Court"], "who_zh": ["约翰·马歇尔", "联邦最高法院"], "what_en": "In Gibbons v. Ogden (1824), the U.S. Supreme Court, headed by Chief Justice John Marshall, voided a New York law that created a monopoly on steamboat travel into New York City, firmly establishing federal authority over interstate commerce.", "what_zh": "1824 年吉本斯诉奥格登案中，由首席大法官约翰·马歇尔领导的联邦最高法院宣布纽约州授予纽约市汽船航运专营权的法律无效，确立了联邦对州际贸易的权威。", "cause_en": "State and national governments were building an interregional network of trade and travel, and local or state monopolies and tariffs threatened to impede the flow of goods, people, and news across the nation.", "cause_zh": "州和联邦政府正在建设跨地区贸易交通网，而地方或州的专营权和关税威胁着全国商品、人员、信息的流通。", "sig_en": "The decision prevented local or state monopolies or tariffs from impeding the national flow of goods, people, and news, clearing the legal path for the Market Revolution's transportation system.", "sig_zh": "该判决防止地方或州专营权、关税阻碍全国商品人员信息流通，为市场革命的交通体系扫清了法律障碍。", "exp_en": "Gibbons v. Ogden gave the federal government the commerce-clause power to keep interstate trade free of state barriers.", "exp_zh": "吉本斯案赋予联邦政府以贸易条款权力，保障州际贸易不受各州壁垒阻碍。", "page": 296, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2838", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.296"}}, {"id": "p4-010", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The Market Revolution and Its Distinction from the Industrial Revolution", "topic_zh": "市场革命及其与工业革命的区别", "year": null, "year_text": "c. 1820-1860", "who": ["merchants", "legislators", "businessmen"], "who_zh": ["商人", "立法者", "企业家"], "what_en": "As factories and farms churned out more goods, legislators and businessmen built canals, roads, steamboats, and railroads to get products to consumers, setting in motion a Market Revolution - the expansion of commerce - alongside the Industrial Revolution, a new system of production based on water and steam power and machine technology. The Market Revolution exploited advances in transportation and business organization to expand trade in farm products and manufactured goods, linking Atlantic states with the trans-Appalachian west.", "what_zh": "随着工厂农场产量激增，立法者和企业家修建运河、公路、汽船和铁路把产品送到消费者手中，发动了市场革命——商业的扩张——与工业革命（以水力蒸汽动力和机械技术为基础的新生产体系）并行。市场革命利用交通和商业组织的进步，扩大了农产品和制成品贸易，把大西洋沿岸各州与阿巴拉契亚以西连接起来。", "cause_en": "Increased factory and farm output needed wider markets; the transportation revolution of canals, steamboats, and later railroads made long-distance trade cheap and fast.", "cause_zh": "工厂农场增产需要更广阔的市场；运河、汽船乃至铁路的交通革命使长途贸易又便宜又快。", "sig_en": "The Market Revolution created regional ties between the Northeast and Midwest, spawned western commercial cities like Chicago and Cincinnati, and drew about 5 million people to lands west of the Appalachians by the 1840s - while its commercial values alarmed critics like Emerson.", "sig_zh": "市场革命缔造了东北与中西部的地区纽带，催生了芝加哥、辛辛那提等西部商业城市，到 1840 年代吸引约 500 万人迁往阿巴拉契亚以西；其商业价值观也引起爱默生等批评者的警惕。", "exp_en": "The Industrial Revolution increased production; the Market Revolution expanded commerce - together they transformed the American economy between 1800 and 1860.", "exp_zh": "工业革命扩大了生产，市场革命扩大了商业——两者共同在 1800 至 1860 年间改造了美国经济。", "page": 293, "src": {"text": "The invasion of Nature by Trade with its Money, its Credit, its Steam, [and] its Railroad threatens to . . . establish a new, universal Monarchy.", "attr": "Ralph Waldo Emerson (1839)"}}, {"id": "p4-011", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Cyrus McCormick and the Mechanical Reaper", "topic_zh": "塞勒斯·麦考密克与机械收割机", "year": 1846, "year_text": "1846", "who": ["Cyrus McCormick"], "who_zh": ["塞勒斯·麦考密克"], "what_en": "In Chicago, Cyrus McCormick used steam-driven machines to make parts for farm reapers, which workers assembled on a conveyor belt. Midwestern companies such as McCormick and Hussey mass-produced self-raking reapers that harvested 12 acres of grain a day, compared with the 2 acres an adult worker could cut; a farmer and his son with a reaper and a horse could cut as much grain in a day as seven men with scythes. In 1846, McCormick moved his reaper factory from western Virginia to Chicago to be closer to his midwestern customers.", "what_zh": "在芝加哥，塞勒斯·麦考密克用蒸汽驱动的机器制造农用收割机零件，工人再在传送带上组装。麦考密克、哈西等中西部公司大批量生产自动耙式收割机，一天可收 12 英亩粮食，而成年工人一天只能割 2 英亩；一个农民带着儿子、一匹马和一台收割机，一天割的粮食相当于七个拿镰刀的人。1846 年，麦考密克把收割机厂从西弗吉尼亚迁到芝加哥，靠近中西部客户。", "cause_en": "Midwestern farmers needed to harvest ever-larger wheat acreages on the prairies, where hand labor could not keep up with planting.", "cause_zh": "中西部农民需要在大草原上收割越来越多的麦田，手工劳动跟不上播种面积的扩张。", "sig_en": "The reaper let farmers plant more acres without fear that wheat would sprout and become worthless before harvest, sharply raising farm productivity and helping Chicago and the Midwest become manufacturing and agricultural centers.", "sig_zh": "收割机让农民放心扩大播种面积，不用担心小麦在收割前发芽报废，大幅提高了农业生产率，助推芝加哥和中西部成为制造与农业中心。", "exp_en": "McCormick's reaper mechanized grain harvesting, making large-scale prairie farming profitable and feeding the Market Revolution's commercial cities.", "exp_zh": "麦考密克的收割机使粮食收割机械化，让大草原大规模种植有利可图，并为市场革命的商业城市提供粮食。", "page": 300, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2853", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.300"}}, {"id": "p4-012", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The Middle Class and the Self-Made Man", "topic_zh": "中产阶级与“白手起家的人”", "year": null, "year_text": "1830s-1840s", "who": ["Benjamin Franklin", "Hezekiah Niles"], "who_zh": ["本杰明·富兰克林", "赫泽凯亚·奈尔斯"], "what_en": "Between wealthy owners and propertyless wage earners grew a middle class - the social product of increased commerce - made up of farmers, mechanics, manufacturers, traders, professionals such as lawyers and contractors, middling business owners, and white-collar clerks; in the Northeast they numbered about 30 percent of the population in the 1840s. Per capita income rose about 2.5 percent a year between 1830 and 1857. Benjamin Franklin's Autobiography, published in full in 1818, gave the classic expression of the secular work ethic, and the self-made man became a central theme of American popular culture - for example, Philadelphia housepainter Warner Myers rose from poverty to build and sell sixty houses.", "what_zh": "在富有的厂主和无产的雇佣工人之间，成长起一个中产阶级——商业扩张的社会产物——包括农民、技工、制造商、商人、律师承包商等专业人士、中等企业主和白领职员；1840 年代东北部约 30% 的人口属于这一阶层。1830 至 1857 年人均收入年均增长约 2.5%。1818 年完整出版的富兰克林《自传》是世俗工作伦理的经典表达，“白手起家的人”成为美国大众文化的中心主题——如费城油漆工沃纳·迈尔斯从赤贫起家，最终建造并售出 60 栋房子。", "cause_en": "Rising prosperity from the Industrial and Market revolutions and an abundance of inexpensive mass-produced goods created a distinct urban culture of material comfort and moral discipline.", "cause_zh": "工商业革命带来的繁荣和大量廉价机制商品，造就了一种讲求物质舒适与道德自律的独特城市文化。", "sig_en": "Just as the yeoman ethic had served as a unifying ideal in pre-1800 agrarian America, the gospel of personal achievement linked the middle and business classes of the new industrializing society.", "sig_zh": "正如自耕农伦理曾是 1800 年前农业美国的统一理想，个人奋斗的福音把新兴工业化社会的中产阶级和商业精英联结在一起。", "exp_en": "The middle class and the self-made man ideal gave industrial America a new social ladder and a moral justification for capitalist success.", "exp_zh": "中产阶级和白手起家的理想为工业美国提供了新的社会阶梯，也为资本主义成功提供了道德辩护。", "page": 302, "src": {"text": "almost universal ambition to get forward", "attr": "Hezekiah Niles, editor of Niles' Weekly Register"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2859", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.302"}}, {"id": "p4-013", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The Benevolent Empire, the American Temperance Society, and Lyman Beecher", "topic_zh": "慈善帝国、美国禁酒协会与莱曼·比彻", "year": null, "year_text": "1820s-1840s", "who": ["Lyman Beecher", "Congregational and Presbyterian ministers"], "who_zh": ["莱曼·比彻", "公理会和长老会牧师"], "what_en": "Led by Congregational and Presbyterian ministers such as Lyman Beecher, the Benevolent Empire - prominent in the 1820s - created organizations of conservative social reform with managing staffs, hundreds of chapters, thousands of volunteers, and newspapers: the Prison Discipline Society, the American Society for the Promotion of Temperance, and the General Union for Promoting the Observance of the Christian Sabbath (1828). Their goal was to restore the moral government of God by reducing alcohol and other vices. Temperance was the most successful reform: evangelical Protestants took over the American Temperance Society in 1832, which grew to two thousand chapters and more than 200,000 members, and spirit consumption fell from an average of 5 gallons per person in 1830 to 2 gallons in 1845.", "what_zh": "以莱曼·比彻为代表的公理会和长老会牧师领导了 1820 年代兴起的“慈善帝国”，创办了一批保守社会改革组织——监狱纪律协会、美国禁酒促进会、1828 年的基督教安息日促进总会——每个组织都有专职人员、数百个分会、数千志愿者和自己的报纸，目标是恢复“上帝的道德治理”，减少酗酒等恶习。禁酒是最成功的改革：1832 年福音派新教徒接管美国禁酒协会，会员增至 2000 个分会、20 多万人；人均烈酒消费量从 1830 年的 5 加仑降到 1845 年的 2 加仑。", "cause_en": "Disorder among wage earners - drunkenness, brawls, crime - alarmed the rising middle classes, who wanted safe cities and a disciplined workforce.", "cause_zh": "雇佣工人中的酗酒、斗殴、犯罪等失序现象让崛起的中产阶级深感不安——他们想要安全的城市和守纪律的劳动力。", "sig_en": "The Benevolent Empire invented large-scale, chapter-based moral reform organizations; temperance dramatically cut drinking and, with religious discipline, bonded middle-class and wage-earning Americans amid industrialization's divisions.", "sig_zh": "慈善帝国发明了大规模分会制的道德改革组织模式；禁酒运动大幅降低饮酒量，并以宗教纪律把中产阶级和工薪阶层凝聚在一起，应对工业化带来的社会分裂。", "why_term": "moral government of God", "why_term_q": "慈善帝国改革者宣称要恢复的（关键词）是 ______。", "exp_en": "Benevolent reformers tried to control working-class behavior through persuasion or law, making moral reform a middle-class project.", "exp_zh": "慈善改革者试图以劝说或法律约束工人阶级的行为，使道德改革成为中产阶级的事业。", "page": 305}, {"id": "p4-014", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Charles Grandison Finney and the Rochester Revivals (1830)", "topic_zh": "查尔斯·芬尼与罗切斯特复兴运动", "year": 1830, "year_text": "1830", "who": ["Charles Grandison Finney", "Lydia Finney"], "who_zh": ["查尔斯·格兰迪森·芬尼", "莉迪亚·芬尼"], "what_en": "Presbyterian minister Charles Grandison Finney, born into a poor Connecticut farming family, underwent an intense religious experience in 1823 and chose the ministry. Beginning in towns along the Erie Canal, he conducted emotional revival meetings stressing conversion over doctrine, repudiating Calvinism and preaching that God would welcome any sinner who submitted to the Holy Spirit. His central message was that God has made man a moral free agent who could choose salvation. His greatest triumph came in 1830 in Rochester, New York, where he preached every day for six months and won over the city's merchants and manufacturers, who promised to attend church, give up intoxicating beverages, and work hard; businessmen founded a Free Presbyterian Church, free because members did not pay for pew space.", "what_zh": "长老会牧师查尔斯·芬尼出身康涅狄格贫苦农家，1823 年经历强烈的宗教体验后投身传教。他从伊利运河沿岸城镇开始举办情感强烈的复兴集会，强调皈依而非教义，否定加尔文主义，宣讲上帝会接纳任何顺服圣灵的罪人。他的核心信息是：上帝赋予人道德自由意志，人可以选择得救。1830 年他在纽约罗切斯特达到巅峰：连续六个月天天布道，赢得全城商人和制造商，他们承诺上教堂、戒酒、勤奋工作；富商们创办了免费长老会教堂（“免费”指座位不收费）。", "cause_en": "Finney's ministry drew on and accelerated the Second Great Awakening, the wave of Protestant revivalism that had begun after the Revolution, amid the social upheaval of the Market Revolution.", "cause_zh": "芬尼的事工借助并加速了第二次大觉醒——革命后兴起的新教复兴浪潮，正值市场革命的社会剧变之际。", "sig_en": "Finney's free-will doctrine appealed to the new middle class's sense of personal responsibility, and his revivals spread from New England to the Midwest, changing the customs of society and feeding temperance and benevolent reform movements.", "sig_zh": "芬尼的自由意志教义契合新兴中产阶级的个人责任感；他的复兴运动从新英格兰蔓延到中西部，改变了社会风俗，并滋养了禁酒和慈善改革运动。", "why_term": "moral free agency", "why_term_q": "芬尼的核心教义、强调人能自由选择得救的（关键词）是 ______。", "exp_en": "Finney democratized salvation through free will and turned revivalism into a disciplined engine of middle-class reform.", "exp_zh": "芬尼以自由意志使救赎民主化，把复兴运动变成了中产阶级改革的有纪律的引擎。", "page": 305}, {"id": "p4-015", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Nativist Movements and Anti-Catholic Riots (1834-1844)", "topic_zh": "本土主义运动与反天主教骚乱", "year": null, "year_text": "1834-1844", "who": ["Samuel F. B. Morse", "Lyman Beecher", "Irish and German Catholic immigrants"], "who_zh": ["塞缪尔·F·B·莫尔斯", "莱曼·比彻", "爱尔兰和德国天主教移民"], "what_en": "Between 1840 and 1860, about 2 million Irish, 1.5 million Germans, and 750,000 Britons poured into the United States; Irish peasants were fleeing a famine caused by overpopulation and a blight that destroyed the potato crop. Confronted by Catholic immigrants, American-born citizens formed nativist movements asserting Protestant superiority. In 1834 Samuel F. B. Morse published Foreign Conspiracy Against the Liberties of the United States, warning of a Catholic threat to republican institutions - it became the nativists' handbook. In 1834 in Charlestown, Massachusetts, a quarrel between Catholic laborers and Protestant workers exploded into a riot that destroyed a convent; in 1844 in Philadelphia, riots erupted when the Catholic bishop persuaded schools to use both Catholic and Protestant Bibles, and anti-Irish violence by nativist clubs escalated into open warfare between Protestants and the Pennsylvania militia.", "what_zh": "1840 至 1860 年，约 200 万爱尔兰人、150 万德国人和 75 万英国人涌入美国；爱尔兰农民为逃避人口过剩和马铃薯枯萎病造成的饥荒而来。面对天主教移民，土生美国人组成本土主义运动，宣扬新教优越。1834 年，塞缪尔·莫尔斯出版《针对美国自由的外国阴谋》，警告天主教威胁共和制度，成为本土主义者的手册。同年在马萨诸塞州查尔斯顿，天主教劳工与新教工人的争吵演变为摧毁修道院的骚乱；1844 年费城，天主教主教说服公立学校同时使用天主教和新教圣经，引发骚乱，本土主义俱乐部的反爱尔兰暴力升级为新教徒与宾州民兵的公开交战。", "cause_en": "Unemployed Protestant mechanics and factory workers accused Catholic immigrants of taking jobs and driving down wages; benevolent Protestants opposed tax funding for Catholic schools and condemned Irish rowdiness; ministers like Beecher warned that Catholic hierarchy was incompatible with republicanism.", "cause_zh": "失业的新教技工和厂工指责天主教移民抢工作、压低工资；慈善派新教徒反对用税款资助天主教学校、谴责爱尔兰人的粗野；比彻等牧师警告天主教等级制与共和主义不相容。", "sig_en": "Religious and cultural tensions divided American society along lines of ethnicity and religion as well as class, and cultural conflicts undercut trade unionism because many Protestant wage earners sided with Protestant employers over Catholic coworkers.", "sig_zh": "宗教文化紧张使美国社会在阶级之外又按族裔和宗教分裂；文化冲突削弱了工会运动，因为许多新教雇佣工人站在新教雇主一边而非天主教工友一边。", "exp_en": "Nativism turned immigration-driven diversity into violent conflict, revealing the limits of republican unity in an industrializing society.", "exp_zh": "本土主义把移民带来的多样性变成暴力冲突，暴露了工业化社会中共和团结的局限。", "page": 310, "src": {"text": "[Catholicism is] a religion which never prospered but in alliance with despotic governments, has always been and still is the inflexible enemy of Liberty of conscience and free inquiry, and at this moment is the main stay of the battle against republican institutions.", "attr": "Lyman Beecher, A Plea for the West (1835)"}}, {"id": "p4-016", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Martin Van Buren and the New York political machine", "topic_zh": "马丁·范布伦与纽约政治机器", "year": 1817, "year_text": "1817–1821", "who": ["Martin Van Buren"], "who_zh": ["马丁·范布伦"], "what_en": "Between 1817 and 1821, Martin Van Buren turned his 'Bucktail' supporters into the first statewide political machine in New York. He bought the Albany Argus newspaper to promote his policies, used patronage as his chief tool, and after the Bucktails won the legislature in 1821 appointed some six thousand supporters to offices. He enforced disciplined voting through a party caucus.", "what_zh": "1817–1821 年间，马丁·范布伦把“雄鹿尾”（Bucktail）支持者打造成纽约州第一个全州政治机器：买下《奥尔巴尼纪事报》宣传政策、以官职恩惠为主要工具，1821 年赢得州议会后任命约六千名亲信为官，并通过党团会议实行严格的投票纪律。", "cause_en": "As the power of notables waned, Van Buren repudiated his dependence on the Van Ness gentry family and set out to build a political order based on party identity, arguing that parties checked an elected official's inherent 'disposition to abuse power.'", "cause_zh": "随着名流权势衰落，范布伦摆脱对范内斯绅士家族的依附，决心建立以政党认同为基础的政治秩序，认为政党能制约官员与生俱来的“滥用权力倾向”。", "sig_en": "Van Buren became the chief architect of party government and the model for Jackson's later national party; critics called his distribution of offices a spoils system, though he defended it as fair and republican.", "sig_zh": "范布伦成为政党政府的主要设计者，为杰克逊后来的全国政党提供样板；批评者称其分官做法为“分赃制度”，他则辩称这是公平且共和的。", "exp_en": "Van Buren justified parties against the old republican fear of factions: they were 'inseparable from free government.' His machine wove together diverse interests and relied on patronage and caucus discipline — the template of the Second Party System.", "exp_zh": "范布伦反驳了共和传统对派系的恐惧：政党与自由政府“不可分割”。他的机器把多元利益编织在一起，靠恩惠与党团纪律运转，成为第二政党体制的样板。", "page": 317, "src": {"text": "All men of sense know that political parties are inseparable from free government,", "attr": "Martin Van Buren"}}, {"id": "p4-017", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Election of 1824 and the 'corrupt bargain'", "topic_zh": "1824 年大选与“腐败交易”", "year": 1824, "year_text": "1824–1825", "who": ["Andrew Jackson", "John Quincy Adams", "Henry Clay", "William H. Crawford"], "who_zh": ["安德鲁·杰克逊", "约翰·昆西·亚当斯", "亨利·克莱", "威廉·克劳福德"], "what_en": "Five Republicans ran for president in 1824. Jackson won 99 electoral votes to Adams's 84, Crawford's 41, and Clay's 37, but no one had a majority, so the House chose among the top three under the Twelfth Amendment. Speaker Henry Clay assembled a coalition that made Adams president in 1825; Adams then named Clay secretary of state, and Jackson's supporters denounced the deal as a corrupt bargain.", "what_zh": "1824 年五位共和党人竞选总统：杰克逊 99 张选举人票，亚当斯 84 张，克劳福德 41 张，克莱 37 张，无人过半。根据第十二修正案，众议院在前三名中抉择；议长克莱组建联盟使亚当斯 1825 年当选，亚当斯随即任命克莱为国务卿，杰克逊派谴责此为“腐败交易”。", "cause_en": "The Federalist Party had disappeared and the Republican Party splintered into factions, while democratic reforms meant eighteen of twenty-four states chose electors by popular vote, letting candidates bypass the congressional caucus.", "cause_zh": "联邦党消失、共和党分裂成派系，同时民主改革使 24 州中有 18 州以普选产生选举人，候选人得以绕开国会党团直接诉诸选民。", "sig_en": "The charge of a corrupt bargain poisoned Adams's presidency, united Jackson's followers in opposition, and helped Jackson win in 1828; it also split the Republicans into the Democrats and the Whigs.", "sig_zh": "“腐败交易”指控毒化了亚当斯的总统任期，使杰克逊支持者团结反对，助杰克逊 1828 年获胜，也导致共和党分裂为民主党与辉格党。", "why_term": "corrupt bargain", "why_term_q": "Jackson 支持者如何称呼 Adams 当选总统、任命 Clay 为国务卿的政治交易？", "exp_en": "Though Jackson led in both popular (43.1%) and electoral votes, the House procedure hurt him because congressmen feared the 'military chieftain.' The bargain accusation became the Democrats' founding grievance.", "exp_zh": "尽管杰克逊在普选（43.1%）和选举人票上都领先，众议院程序对他不利，因为议员们惧怕这位“军阀”。“腐败交易”指控成为民主党的建党 grievance（怨愤之源）。", "page": 319, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2900", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.319"}}, {"id": "p4-018", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Henry Clay's American System", "topic_zh": "亨利·克莱的“美洲体系”", "year": 1825, "year_text": "1825", "who": ["Henry Clay", "John Quincy Adams"], "who_zh": ["亨利·克莱", "约翰·昆西·亚当斯"], "what_en": "Clay's American System was an integrated mercantilist program of national economic development with three elements: protective tariffs to stimulate manufacturing, federally subsidized internal improvements (roads and canals), and a national bank to control credit and provide a uniform currency. President Adams endorsed it as his central policy.", "what_zh": "克莱的“美洲体系”是一套国家经济发展的重商主义综合方案，含三要素：保护性关税刺激制造业、联邦资助的国内改进（道路运河）、国家银行控制信贷并提供统一货币。亚当斯总统将其作为核心政策背书。", "cause_en": "The West needed better transportation and manufacturers wanted protection from British imports, while Clay and Adams believed in bold national action to 'improve the conditions' of Americans.", "cause_zh": "西部需要更好的交通，制造业者希望抵御英国进口竞争，克莱与亚当斯相信联邦应采取大胆行动“改善”国民境况。", "sig_en": "The program won praise in the West but sharp criticism in the South, which relied on rivers and had few industries to protect; Jackson later made destroying the American System his highest priority.", "sig_zh": "该方案在西部受赞誉，在南方遭强烈批评（南方靠河流运棉、花无工业需保护）；杰克逊后来把摧毁美洲体系作为首要目标。", "exp_en": "William Crawford denounced the System as a scheme to 'consolidate' power in Washington, and Madison-style constitutional objections helped Van Buren defeat most of Adams's road and canal subsidies.", "exp_zh": "克劳福德谴责该体系是把权力“集中”到华盛顿的阴谋；麦迪逊式的宪法异议帮助范布伦否决了亚当斯多数道路运河补贴。", "page": 319, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2900", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.319"}}, {"id": "p4-019", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Tariff of Abominations (1828)", "topic_zh": "“可憎关税”（1828）", "year": 1828, "year_text": "1828", "who": ["northern Jacksonians", "southern planters"], "who_zh": ["北方杰克逊派", "南方种植园主"], "what_en": "The Tariff of 1828 raised duties significantly on raw materials, textiles, and iron goods. It enraged the South, which produced the world's cheapest raw cotton and needed no protection: planters had to buy either costlier American goods or highly dutied British imports, costing them about $100 million a year. An Alabama legislator called it 'little less than legalized pillage.'", "what_zh": "1828 年关税大幅提高原材料、纺织品和铁制品的税率，激怒南方：南方生产世界最便宜的原棉、无需保护，种植园主只能买更贵的美国货或高税英国货，每年损失约 1 亿美元。一位亚拉巴马议员称之为“无异于合法抢劫”。", "cause_en": "Van Buren and his Jacksonian allies hopped on the tariff bandwagon, raising duties on wool and hemp to win farmers in New York, Ohio, and Kentucky for Jackson's 1828 candidacy — the tariff became 'a machine for manufacturing Presidents.'", "cause_zh": "范布伦和杰克逊派搭上关税顺风车，提高羊毛大麻税率以争取纽约、俄亥俄、肯塔基农民支持杰克逊 1828 年竞选——关税成了“制造总统的机器”。", "sig_en": "Ignoring the Jacksonians' role, most southerners blamed President Adams; the tariff's burden on the South directly triggered the nullification crisis.", "sig_zh": "南方人无视杰克逊派的作用，把账算在亚当斯头上；关税对南方的重负直接引发了废止权危机。", "exp_en": "The tariff battle showed how economic policy became a political weapon: northern Jacksonians joined Adams and Clay supporters to enact it, then Jackson inherited the southern fury it created.", "exp_zh": "关税之争显示经济政策如何沦为政治武器：北方杰克逊派联手亚当斯、克莱支持者通过法案，杰克逊却继承了它激起的南方怒火。", "page": 320, "src": {"text": "little less than legalized pillage,", "attr": "an Alabama legislator"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2904", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.320"}}, {"id": "p4-020", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Election of 1828 and 'The Democracy'", "topic_zh": "1828 年大选与“民主派”", "year": 1828, "year_text": "1828", "who": ["Andrew Jackson", "Martin Van Buren", "John C. Calhoun"], "who_zh": ["安德鲁·杰克逊", "马丁·范布伦", "约翰·卡尔霍恩"], "what_en": "Van Buren revived Jefferson's coalition of southern planters and northern farmers and artisans, with Calhoun as Jackson's running mate. The Jacksonians called themselves Democrats or 'the Democracy.' Over 1.1 million men voted — more than three times the 1824 total — and 56 percent chose Jackson (178 electoral votes to Adams's 83), the first president from a trans-Appalachian state.", "what_zh": "范布伦重建了杰斐逊的南方种植园主加北方农民工匠联盟，卡尔霍恩为杰克逊竞选搭档。杰克逊派自称民主党人或“民主派”。110 多万人投票（为 1824 年三倍多），56% 选杰克逊（178 对 83 张选举人票），他是首位来自阿巴拉契亚山以西的总统。", "cause_en": "Jackson's frontier origins and rise symbolized the democratic age; his hostility to corporations and the American System won artisans and workers, while his 'judicious' tariff stance and Indian-removal record kept the South and West loyal.", "cause_zh": "杰克逊的边疆出身与崛起象征民主时代；他敌视公司与美洲体系赢得工匠工人，对关税“明智”表态及印第安人迁移立场保住南部与西部。", "sig_en": "Voter participation soared (from about one-quarter in 1824 to over one-half), the disciplined national Democratic Party was born, and Jackson used his popular mandate to transform the presidency.", "sig_zh": "投票率飙升（1824 年约四分之一到 1828 年过半），纪律严明的全国民主党诞生，杰克逊凭借民意授权改造了总统职位。", "exp_en": "Jackson's ally Duff Green hoped the national party would put 'the anti-slave party in the North ... to sleep for twenty years to come' — the party bargain that kept slavery off the national agenda.", "exp_zh": "杰克逊盟友达夫·格林希望全国政党能让“北方的反奴隶制派……再睡二十年”——这是把奴隶制排除出全国议程的政党交易。", "page": 321, "src": {"text": "equality among the people in the rights conferred by government", "attr": "Andrew Jackson"}}, {"id": "p4-021", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Spoils system and rotation in office", "topic_zh": "分赃制度与官员轮换制", "year": 1829, "year_text": "1829", "who": ["Andrew Jackson", "William L. Marcy"], "who_zh": ["安德鲁·杰克逊", "威廉·马西"], "what_en": "Following Van Buren's New York example, Jackson used patronage to create a disciplined national party. He rejected 'property in office' and insisted on rotation of officeholders with each new administration, claiming public duties were 'so plain and simple that men of intelligence may readily qualify themselves for their performance.' New York Jacksonian William L. Marcy put it bluntly: 'to the victor belong the spoils of the enemy.'", "what_zh": "效仿范布伦在纽约的做法，杰克逊用官职恩惠打造纪律严明的全国政党。他否定“官职私有”，坚持每届新政府轮换官员，称公务“简单明了，有才智者皆可胜任”。纽约杰克逊派威廉·马西直言：“胜者得战利品。”", "cause_en": "Jackson believed rotation was democratic and would prevent a permanent office-holding elite, while patronage rewarded allies and secured backing for his policies.", "cause_zh": "杰克逊认为轮换是民主的、可防止官职世袭精英，同时恩惠能奖赏盟友、为政策争取支持。", "sig_en": "The spoils system staffed the growing federal bureaucracy with party loyalists and became the organizational backbone of the Second Party System — and of its corruption.", "sig_zh": "分赃制度使日益庞大的联邦官僚机构充斥政党亲信，成为第二政党体制的组织支柱——也是其腐败之源。", "exp_en": "Critics had already called Van Buren's 1821 distribution of six thousand New York offices a spoils system; Jackson nationalized the practice and defended it as thoroughly republican because it reflected the majority's will.", "exp_zh": "批评者早已把范布伦 1821 年分发六千个纽约官职的做法称为分赃；杰克逊将其全国化，并辩称它反映多数人意志、完全共和。", "page": 323, "src": {"text": "to the victor belong the spoils of the enemy.", "attr": "William L. Marcy"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2914", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.323"}}, {"id": "p4-022", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Nullification crisis (1828–1833)", "topic_zh": "废止权危机（1828–1833）", "year": 1832, "year_text": "1828–1833", "who": ["John C. Calhoun", "Andrew Jackson", "Daniel Webster"], "who_zh": ["约翰·卡尔霍恩", "安德鲁·杰克逊", "丹尼尔·韦伯斯特"], "what_en": "Vice President John C. Calhoun anonymously wrote The South Carolina Exposition and Protest (1828), arguing a state convention could void a congressional law. In November 1832 South Carolina adopted an Ordinance of Nullification declaring the tariffs of 1828 and 1832 null and void, barring collection after February 1, 1833, and threatening secession. Jackson warned 'Disunion by armed force is treason,' won a Force Bill in early 1833, and signed a compromise tariff cutting rates to 1816 levels over a decade; South Carolina then dropped its constitutional stand.", "what_zh": "副总统卡尔霍恩匿名撰写《南卡罗来纳州陈述与抗议》（1828），主张州制宪会议可宣布国会法律无效。1832 年 11 月南卡通过《废止条例》，宣布 1828 与 1832 年关税无效，1833 年 2 月 1 日后禁止征税，并威胁脱离联邦。杰克逊警告“以武力分裂即叛国”，1833 年初赢得《武力法案》，并签署妥协关税（十年内税率降至 1816 年水平）；南卡随后放弃宪法立场。", "cause_en": "High-tariff congressmen reenacted the Tariff of Abominations in 1832; South Carolina's slave owners — a black-majority state fearing rebellion and abolition after Britain's 1833 emancipation — attacked the tariff to lower rates and discourage federal power over slavery.", "cause_zh": "高关税派议员 1832 年重立“可憎关税”；南卡奴隶主（黑人占多数的州，恐惧叛乱，又因英国 1833 年废奴而担心联邦干预奴隶制）借攻击关税来降税并遏制联邦权力。", "sig_en": "Jackson upheld national authority by threatening military force while cutting the tariff — the constitutional principle Abraham Lincoln would embrace in the 1861 secession crisis.", "sig_zh": "杰克逊以武力威胁维护国家权威，同时降低关税——这一宪法原则后来被林肯在 1861 年脱离危机中继承。", "why_term": "Liberty and Union, now and forever, one and inseparable!", "why_term_q": "1830 年 Webster-Hayne 辩论中，Webster 名垂青史的结语是 ______。", "exp_en": "Calhoun built on Jefferson and Madison's Kentucky and Virginia Resolutions of 1798 (sovereignty lies in the states); Webster answered with a nationalist celebration of popular sovereignty in the famous 1830 Senate debate with Robert Y. Hayne.", "exp_zh": "卡尔霍恩继承杰斐逊、麦迪逊 1798 年肯塔基与弗吉尼亚决议（主权在州）；韦伯斯特则在 1830 年与海恩的著名参议院辩论中以民族主义的人民主权论回应。", "page": 324, "src": {"text": "Disunion by armed force is treason.", "attr": "Andrew Jackson"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2917", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.324"}}, {"id": "p4-023", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Second Bank of the United States and the Bank War", "topic_zh": "第二合众国银行与银行战争", "year": 1832, "year_text": "1832–1836", "who": ["Andrew Jackson", "Nicholas Biddle", "Henry Clay", "Roger B. Taney"], "who_zh": ["安德鲁·杰克逊", "尼古拉斯·比德尔", "亨利·克莱", "罗杰·托尼"], "what_en": "In 1832 Clay and Webster persuaded bank president Nicholas Biddle to seek an early recharter of the Second Bank (founded 1816, twenty-year charter). Jackson vetoed it, declaring Congress had no constitutional authority for a national bank and condemning the bank as a privileged monopoly. He won reelection 219 to 49 electoral votes, had Taney transfer federal deposits to 'pet banks' in 1833, survived a Senate censure in March 1834, and killed the bank when its charter expired in 1836.", "what_zh": "1832 年克莱与韦伯斯特说服行长比德尔提前申请第二银行（1816 年成立，二十年特许）续期。杰克逊否决，宣称国会无权设立国家银行，谴责其为特权垄断。他以 219 对 49 张选举人票连任，1833 年让托尼把联邦存款转入“宠物银行”，顶住 1834 年 3 月参议院谴责，1836 年特许到期时终结了该银行。", "cause_en": "Clay and Webster hoped a veto would split the Democrats before the 1832 election; Jackson genuinely believed the bank was unconstitutional, 'subversive of the rights of the States,' and owned partly by British aristocrats.", "cause_zh": "克莱与韦伯斯特希望否决能在 1832 年大选前分裂民主党；杰克逊则真心认为银行违宪、“颠覆各州权利”，且部分股权在英国贵族手中。", "sig_en": "Jackson destroyed both national banking and the American System, producing a profound check on federal economic activism: 'All is gone, which the General Government was instituted to create and preserve.'", "sig_zh": "杰克逊摧毁了国家银行与美洲体系，对联邦经济干预造成深远遏制：“凡联邦政府为创设和维护的一切，皆已荡然无存。”", "exp_en": "Jackson's claim that his reelection was 'the decision of the people against the bank' was a new, radical assertion of presidential power — never before had a president claimed an electoral mandate to act independently of Congress.", "exp_zh": "杰克逊声称连任即“人民对银行的裁决”，是前所未有的激进总统权力主张——此前从无总统声称凭选举授权可独立于国会行事。", "page": 326, "src": {"text": "subversive of the rights of the States, dangerous to the liberties of the people", "attr": "Andrew Jackson"}}, {"id": "p4-024", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Indian Removal Act of 1830", "topic_zh": "1830 年《印第安人迁移法》", "year": 1830, "year_text": "1830", "who": ["Andrew Jackson", "Catharine Beecher", "Lydia Sigourney"], "who_zh": ["安德鲁·杰克逊", "凯瑟琳·比彻", "莉迪亚·西格妮"], "what_en": "Jackson pushed the Indian Removal Act through Congress — it squeaked through the House 102 to 97. The act created the Indian Territory on Louisiana Purchase lands in present-day Oklahoma and Kansas, offering money and reserved land to Native peoples who gave up ancestral holdings east of the Mississippi, with promises they could live there 'as long as grass grows and water runs.'", "what_zh": "杰克逊推动《印第安人迁移法》通过国会，众议院以 102 对 97 惊险通过。该法在路易斯安那购地（今俄克拉何马、堪萨斯）设立印第安领地，以金钱和保留地换取密西西比河以东部落的祖居地，承诺他们可“草青水流不息”长居于此。", "cause_en": "White Southerners and Midwesterners demanded resettlement west of the Mississippi; Georgia demanded the federal pledge of 1802 to extinguish Indian titles; Jackson withdrew federal troops protecting Indian enclaves, declaring states sovereign within their borders.", "cause_zh": "南方与中西部白人要求把印第安人迁往密西西比河以西；佐治亚要求兑现 1802 年联邦消灭印第安地权的承诺；杰克逊撤走保护印第安飞地的联邦军队，宣称各州在其边界内拥有主权。", "sig_en": "The act formalized removal as national policy; over the next years scores of Indian peoples were forced west, opening ancestral lands to white settlement.", "sig_zh": "该法使迁移成为国策；随后数年大批印第安部落被迫西迁，祖居地向白人定居开放。", "exp_en": "Evangelical opponents fought hard: Catharine Beecher and Lydia Sigourney's Ladies Circular urged 'benevolent ladies' to petition Congress, and women flooded Congress with petitions — but the bill still passed.", "exp_zh": "福音派反对者奋力抗争：比彻与西格妮的《女士通告》呼吁“仁慈的女士们”向国会请愿，妇女请愿书如潮涌入国会——法案仍获通过。", "page": 327, "src": {"text": "they and all their children, as long as grass grows and water runs.", "attr": "U.S. government officials"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2924", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.327"}}, {"id": "p4-025", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Cherokee Nation v. Georgia (1831) and Worcester v. Georgia (1832)", "topic_zh": "切罗基族诉佐治亚州案（1831）与伍斯特诉佐治亚州案（1832）", "year": 1832, "year_text": "1831–1832", "who": ["John Marshall", "Cherokee Nation"], "who_zh": ["约翰·马歇尔", "切罗基族"], "what_en": "The Cherokees took their land defense to the Supreme Court. In Cherokee Nation v. Georgia (1831), Chief Justice John Marshall denied their claim to 'foreign nation' status, calling Indian peoples 'domestic dependent nations.' But in Worcester v. Georgia (1832), Marshall sided with the Cherokees, voiding Georgia's extension of state law and holding that Indian nations were 'distinct political communities' with exclusive authority guaranteed by the United States.", "what_zh": "切罗基人把土地保卫战打到最高法院。1831 年“切罗基族诉佐治亚州”案中，首席大法官马歇尔否认其“外国”地位，称印第安人为“国内依附民族”。但在 1832 年“伍斯特诉佐治亚州”案中，马歇尔支持切罗基人，废除佐治亚州法律的延伸，裁定印第安民族是“独特的政治共同体”，其排他性权威受美国保障。", "cause_en": "Georgia had extended state law over the Cherokees and demanded fulfillment of the 1802 federal pledge to extinguish Indian land titles, while the Cherokees — with a written language, a constitution modeled on the U.S., and thriving farms — claimed sovereign rights.", "cause_zh": "佐治亚把州法律延伸到切罗基人头上，并要求兑现 1802 年联邦消灭印第安地权的承诺；而拥有文字、仿美国宪法和兴旺农场的切罗基人主张主权权利。", "sig_en": "Instead of guaranteeing Cherokee territory, the U.S. government took it: officials and a minority faction signed the Treaty of New Echota (1835), and the Cherokees were marched west on the Trail of Tears.", "sig_zh": "美国政府并未保障切罗基领地，反而夺走：官员与少数派签署《新埃科塔条约》（1835），切罗基人被迫踏上“血泪之路”西迁。", "exp_en": "Cherokee assimilation was extensive — Sequoyah's syllabary (1821), a constitutional government (1827), mills, looms, and plantations worked by enslaved blacks — yet even this did not protect their lands.", "exp_zh": "切罗基人的同化程度很深——塞阔雅音节文字（1821）、立宪政府（1827）、磨坊织机和黑奴劳动的种植园——但这仍保不住他们的土地。", "page": 330, "src": {"text": "distinct political communities, having territorial boundaries, within which their authority is exclusive and is guaranteed by the United States.", "attr": "Chief Justice John Marshall"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2930", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.330"}}, {"id": "p4-026", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Bad Axe massacre (1832)", "topic_zh": "巴德阿克斯大屠杀（1832）", "year": 1832, "year_text": "1832", "who": ["Black Hawk"], "who_zh": ["黑鹰"], "what_en": "When Chief Black Hawk and his Sauk and Fox followers refused to leave rich farmland in western Illinois in 1832, Jackson sent troops to expel them. The U.S. Army pursued them into the Wisconsin Territory and, in the brutal eight-hour Bad Axe Massacre, killed 850 of Black Hawk's 1,000 warriors.", "what_zh": "1832 年，黑鹰酋长率索克与福克斯族人拒绝离开伊利诺伊西部肥沃农田，杰克逊派军队驱逐。美军追入威斯康星领地，在残酷的八小时巴德阿克斯大屠杀中杀死黑鹰 1000 名战士中的 850 人。", "cause_en": "Black Hawk mobilized after Congress approved the Indian Removal Act (1830) to protect ancestral lands in Illinois: 'It was here, that I was born — and here lie the bones of many friends and relatives.'", "cause_zh": "国会通过《印第安人迁移法》（1830）后，黑鹰动员族人保卫伊利诺伊祖居地：“我生于斯，亲友之骨亦葬于斯。”", "sig_en": "Over the next five years, American diplomatic pressure and military power forced seventy Indian peoples to sign treaties and move west of the Mississippi.", "sig_zh": "随后五年，美国以外交压力与军事力量迫使七十个印第安部落签约迁往密西西比河以西。", "exp_en": "Bad Axe showed removal was enforced by the Army, not just by treaties: resistance in the Old Northwest was crushed as thoroughly as in the Southeast.", "exp_zh": "巴德阿克斯表明迁移靠军队而非仅靠条约执行：旧西北地区的反抗与东南部一样被彻底镇压。", "page": 330, "src": {"text": "It was here, that I was born — and here lie the bones of many friends and relatives. I never could consent to leave it.", "attr": "Black Hawk"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2930", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.330"}}, {"id": "p4-027", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Whig Party (1834) and the 'log cabin campaign' of 1840", "topic_zh": "辉格党（1834）与 1840 年“小木屋竞选”", "year": 1840, "year_text": "1834–1841", "who": ["Henry Clay", "Daniel Webster", "John C. Calhoun", "William Henry Harrison", "John Tyler"], "who_zh": ["亨利·克莱", "丹尼尔·韦伯斯特", "约翰·卡尔霍恩", "威廉·亨利·哈里森", "约翰·泰勒"], "what_en": "The Whig Party formed in 1834 when congressmen — led by Clay, Webster, and Calhoun — opposed Jackson's policies and 'kinglike' conduct, taking their name from the pre-Revolutionary Whigs who opposed arbitrary monarchs. In 1840 the Whigs ran war hero William Henry Harrison and John Tyler, winning with the 'log cabin campaign' and slogan 'Tippecanoe and Tyler Too!' Harrison died of pneumonia a month after his 1841 inauguration; Tyler took the oath, vetoed Whig bank and tariff bills, and was expelled from the party — 'His Accidency.'", "what_zh": "1834 年，反对杰克逊政策与“帝王式”作风的国会议员（克莱、韦伯斯特、卡尔霍恩领衔）组建辉格党，党名取自革命前反对专制君主的辉格派。1840 年辉格党推出战争英雄哈里森与泰勒，以“小木屋竞选”和口号“蒂珀卡努与泰勒同行！”获胜。哈里森 1841 年就职一月后死于肺炎；泰勒宣誓继任，否决辉格党的银行与关税法案，被开除出党——“意外总统”。", "cause_en": "Whigs accused 'King Andrew I' of violating the Constitution through the spoils system and executive overreach; ex-Anti-Masons (the party born after William Morgan's 1826 murder) and moral reformers swelled their ranks.", "cause_zh": "辉格党指控“安德鲁一世”以分赃制和行政越权违反宪法；前反共济会党人（1826 年摩根被杀后兴起的政党）与道德改革者壮大了其队伍。", "sig_en": "The 1840 campaign pioneered modern mass campaigning — songs, parades, and rallies drew 80 percent turnout — and created the Second Party System; Tyler's succession set the precedent that the vice president becomes full president, while his vetoes wrecked the Whig program.", "sig_zh": "1840 年竞选开创现代大众竞选模式——歌谣、游行、集会带来 80% 投票率，第二政党体制成形；泰勒继任确立副总统继任为正式总统的先例，而他的否决摧毁了辉格党纲领。", "why_term": "Tippecanoe and Tyler Too!", "why_term_q": "1840 年辉格党的竞选口号是 ______。", "exp_en": "Whig imagery was deliberately misleading: Harrison was painted as a log-cabin, hard-cider common man though he lived in elegant mansions, while 'Martin Van Ruin' was mocked as an aristocrat. Women were welcomed to campaign events for the first time in American politics.", "exp_zh": "辉格党形象刻意误导：哈里森被塑造成住小木屋、喝苹果酒的平民，实则住豪宅；“马丁·范毁”被嘲为贵族。这是美国政治史上首次欢迎妇女参加竞选活动。", "page": 332, "src": {"text": "Of the two great parties, the Democracy has the best cause ... for free trade, for wide suffrage, but the Whig Party has the best men.", "attr": "Ralph Waldo Emerson"}}, {"id": "p4-028", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Roger Taney as chief justice and the Charles River Bridge case (1837)", "topic_zh": "托尼任首席大法官与查尔斯河桥案（1837）", "year": 1837, "year_text": "1835–1837", "who": ["Roger B. Taney", "John Marshall"], "who_zh": ["罗杰·托尼", "约翰·马歇尔"], "what_en": "Jackson appointed Roger B. Taney chief justice in 1835 (he served until 1864). In Charles River Bridge Co. v. Warren Bridge Co. (1837), Taney held that a legislative charter to build a toll bridge did not necessarily bestow a monopoly, so a legislature could charter a competing bridge to promote the general welfare: 'While the rights of private property are sacredly guarded, we must not forget that the community also has rights.'", "what_zh": "杰克逊 1835 年任命罗杰·托尼为首席大法官（任职至 1864）。1837 年“查尔斯河桥公司诉沃伦桥公司”案中，托尼裁定立法特许建收费桥并不必然授予垄断权，议会可为公益特许竞争性桥梁：“私有财产权神圣不可侵犯，但我们也不可忘记社会亦有其权利。”", "cause_en": "Jackson sought to undermine Marshall's nationalist, vested-rights jurisprudence and give constitutional legitimacy to his policies of states' rights and free enterprise.", "cause_zh": "杰克逊意在削弱马歇尔的民族主义既得权利法理，为其州权与自由企业政策提供宪法正当性。", "sig_en": "The decision directly challenged Marshall's contract-clause reading in Dartmouth College v. Woodward (1819); by limiting existing canal and turnpike companies' claims, it let legislatures charter competing railroads — cheaper, more efficient transportation. The Taney Court also boosted state power in Mayor of New York v. Miln (1837) and Briscoe v. Bank of Kentucky (1837).", "sig_zh": "该判决直接挑战马歇尔在达特茅斯学院案（1819）中对契约条款的解释；通过限制运河收费公路公司的既有权利，使议会得以特许竞争性铁路——更便宜高效的运输。托尼法院还在 1837 年另两案中强化了州权。", "exp_en": "The Taney Court partially reversed Marshall's nationalism: it enhanced states' regulatory 'police power' and restored economic powers states had held before 1787, while Jacksonian state constitutions (1830–1860) wrote laissez-faire limits on government aid to business.", "exp_zh": "托尼法院部分逆转了马歇尔的民族主义：强化各州规制“警察权”，恢复 1787 年前各州的经济权力；杰克逊时代各州宪法（1830–1860）也把自由放任、限制政府助商写入条文。", "page": 331, "src": {"text": "While the rights of private property are sacredly guarded, we must not forget that the community also has rights.", "attr": "Chief Justice Roger B. Taney"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2933", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.331"}}, {"id": "p4-029", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Panic of 1837 and the Specie Circular", "topic_zh": "1837 年恐慌与《硬币通告》", "year": 1837, "year_text": "1836–1837", "who": ["Martin Van Buren"], "who_zh": ["马丁·范布伦"], "what_en": "The panic began when the Bank of England sharply curtailed the flow of money and credit to the United States and British mills slashed cotton purchases, sending cotton from 20 to 10 cents a pound. On May 8, 1837 the Dry Dock Bank of New York ran out of specie; within two weeks every American bank had stopped paying specie. Jackson's 1836 Specie Circular — requiring only gold and silver for public-land purchases — was mistakenly blamed; the British credit squeeze was the main cause.", "what_zh": "恐慌始于英格兰银行大幅收紧流向美国的货币信贷、英国纺织厂削减购棉，棉价从 20 美分跌至 10 美分。1837 年 5 月 8 日纽约干船坞银行耗尽硬币，两周内全美银行停止兑付。杰克逊 1836 年《硬币通告》（购公地只收金银）被误认为是祸首，实为英国信贷收缩所致。", "cause_en": "Since 1822 British manufacturers had extended credit to southern planters and British investors had bought millions in state canal bonds; suddenly deprived of British funds, Americans had to withdraw gold to pay foreign debts while cotton prices collapsed.", "cause_zh": "1822 年以来英国制造商向南方种植园主放贷、英国投资者购买数百万美元州运河债券；英国资金骤断后，美国人须提取黄金偿外债，棉价同时崩盘。", "sig_en": "The economy fell into a deep depression (1837–1843): nine states defaulted on debts, canal construction fell 90 percent, prices and wages fell 50 percent, unemployment hit 20 percent, and the depression finished off the Working Men's Parties and the union movement.", "sig_zh": "经济陷入深度萧条（1837–1843）：九州债券违约，运河建设下降 90%，物价工资跌 50%，失业率达 20%，萧条终结了工人党与工会运动。", "exp_en": "Van Buren refused to intervene — 'the less government interferes with private pursuits the better for the general prosperity' — and his 1840 Independent Treasury Act, which locked federal specie in government vaults, delayed recovery. Voters blamed the Democrats and elected Harrison.", "exp_zh": "范布伦拒绝干预——“政府越少干预私人经营，公共繁荣越好”；其 1840 年《独立国库法》把联邦硬币锁进政府金库，延缓复苏。选民归罪民主党，选出哈里森。", "page": 334, "src": {"text": "the less government interferes with private pursuits the better for the general prosperity.", "attr": "Martin Van Buren"}}, {"id": "p4-030", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Trail of Tears (1838)", "topic_zh": "血泪之路（1838）", "year": 1838, "year_text": "1838", "who": ["Martin Van Buren", "Winfield Scott", "Cherokee Nation"], "who_zh": ["马丁·范布伦", "温菲尔德·斯科特", "切罗基族"], "what_en": "In 1835 U.S. officials and a minority Cherokee faction signed the Treaty of New Echota, requiring resettlement in Indian Territory. When only 2,000 of 17,000 Cherokees had moved by the May 1838 deadline, President Van Buren ordered General Winfield Scott to enforce the treaty. Scott's army rounded up 14,000 Cherokees and marched them 1,200 miles west; some 3,000 died of starvation and exposure on the journey known as the Trail of Tears.", "what_zh": "1835 年美国官员与切罗基少数派签署《新埃科塔条约》，要求迁往印第安领地。1838 年 5 月期限到时 17000 人中仅 2000 人迁移，范布伦总统命温菲尔德·斯科特将军强制执行。军队围捕 14000 名切罗基人，押送西行 1200 英里，约 3000 人死于饥饿与风寒，是为“血泪之路”。", "cause_en": "The Removal Act of 1830 and the fraudulent New Echota treaty committed the U.S. to clearing the Southeast; the Supreme Court's Worcester ruling in the Cherokees' favor was simply ignored.", "cause_zh": "1830 年《迁移法》与欺诈性的《新埃科塔条约》使美国决意清空东南部；最高法院伍斯特案的有利判决被直接无视。", "sig_en": "The march killed nearly one-fifth of the Cherokee Nation; once in Oklahoma, the Cherokees barred anyone of 'negro or mulatto parentage' from office, affirming a racially defined citizenship — a 'red man's country' mirroring America's 'white man's country.'", "sig_zh": "这次行军夺去近五分之一切罗基人的生命；抵达俄克拉何马后，切罗基人禁止“黑人或混血血统”者任公职，确立种族界定的公民身份——以“红人国度”对应美国的“白人国度”。", "exp_en": "The Creeks, Chickasaws, and Choctaws had moved west under pressure; only the Seminoles, fighting a successful guerrilla war in Florida in the 1840s, kept their lands — the exception to Jacksonian removal.", "exp_zh": "克里克、奇卡索、乔克托族已在压力下西迁；唯有塞米诺尔人在 1840 年代佛罗里达打赢游击战保住土地——成为杰克逊迁移政策的例外。", "page": 331, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2933", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.331"}}, {"id": "p4-031", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Transcendentalism and Ralph Waldo Emerson", "topic_zh": "超验主义与拉尔夫·沃尔多·爱默生", "year": 1832, "year_text": "1832 (Emerson resigns his Boston pulpit and turns to transcendentalism)", "who": ["Ralph Waldo Emerson", "Alexis de Tocqueville"], "who_zh": ["拉尔夫·沃尔多·爱默生", "亚历克西·德·托克维尔"], "what_en": "In 1832 Emerson resigned his Boston pulpit, moved to Concord, Massachusetts, and became the leading voice of transcendentalism, an intellectual movement urging people to shed inherited customs and discover their \"original relation with Nature\" in mystical union with the \"currents of Universal Being.\"", "what_zh": "1832年，爱默生辞去波士顿牧师职务，迁居马萨诸塞州康科德，成为超验主义的领军人物。超验主义主张人们摆脱继承而来的习俗，发现自己与自然的\"本初关系\"，与\"宇宙存在之流\"神秘合一。", "cause_en": "Rapid economic growth and geographic expansion had weakened traditional institutions; New England Unitarian ministers questioning their Puritan heritage turned to European romanticism, which rejected Enlightenment rationalism and held that people could know the infinite through their intuitive powers.", "cause_zh": "经济快速增长与地理扩张削弱了传统制度；质疑清教传统的新英格兰一位论派牧师转向欧洲浪漫主义，后者拒绝启蒙理性主义，主张人可凭直觉认识无限与永恒。", "sig_en": "Emerson's celebration of \"the infinitude of the private man\" shaped middle-class American individualism, inspired a generation of writers such as Thoreau, Fuller, and Whitman, and linked transcendentalism to antislavery and education reform.", "sig_zh": "爱默生对\"私人无限性\"的歌颂塑造了美国中产阶级的个人主义，启发了梭罗、富勒、惠特曼等一代作家，并把超验主义与废奴及教育改革联系起来。", "why_term": "individualism", "why_term_q": "1835年托克维尔创造的、用以描述传统社会纽带松弛的关键词是 ______。", "exp_en": "Transcendentalism was the philosophical core of the era of reform: Emerson turned the liberation of the individual into a creed, spreading it through fifteen hundred lyceum lectures across twenty states.", "exp_zh": "超验主义是改革时代的哲学核心：爱默生把个人解放变成一种信条，通过在二十个州巡回发表的一千五百场讲座传播开来。", "page": 346, "src": {"text": "What is a man born for but to be a Reformer, a Remaker of what man has made?", "attr": "Ralph Waldo Emerson"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2974", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.346"}}, {"id": "p4-032", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Henry David Thoreau and Walden", "topic_zh": "亨利·戴维·梭罗与《瓦尔登湖》", "year": 1845, "year_text": "1845 (Thoreau moves to Walden Pond); Walden published 1854", "who": ["Henry David Thoreau"], "who_zh": ["亨利·戴维·梭罗"], "what_en": "In 1845 Thoreau built a cabin near Walden Pond in Concord and lived alone for two years seeking meaning beyond the artificiality of civilized society; his 1854 Walden justified independent thinking — \"If a man does not keep pace with his companions, perhaps it is because he hears a different drummer\" — and urged peaceful resistance to unjust laws.", "what_zh": "1845年梭罗在康科德瓦尔登湖畔建起小屋，独居两年，在文明社会的人工性之外寻找意义。他1854年出版的《瓦尔登湖》为独立思考辩护——\"如果一个人跟不上同伴的步伐，也许是因为他听到了不同的鼓点\"，并主张以和平方式反抗不公正的法律。", "cause_en": "Heeding Emerson's \"American Scholar\" (1837) call to free American authors from the \"courtly muse\" of Old Europe, and depressed by his brother's death, Thoreau sought inspiration directly from the natural world.", "cause_zh": "梭罗响应了爱默生1837年《美国学者》中\"摆脱旧欧洲宫廷缪斯\"的号召，又因兄长之死而抑郁，转而直接从自然界寻找灵感。", "sig_en": "Walden became an enduring justification for individualism and civil disobedience; Thoreau's refusal to pay taxes over the Mexican War led to his 1848 essay \"Resistance to Civil Government,\" urging individuals to follow a higher moral law.", "sig_zh": "《瓦尔登湖》成为个人主义与公民抗命的经典依据；梭罗因反对美墨战争而拒缴税款，写下1848年散文《论公民的不服从》，主张个人服从更高的道德律。", "exp_en": "Thoreau carried transcendental individualism to its practical extreme: live deliberately, conform to nothing unthinkingly, and resist the unjust state.", "exp_zh": "梭罗把超验主义的个人主义推向实践极致：审慎地生活、不盲从任何习俗、反抗不公正的国家。", "page": 347, "src": {"text": "I went to the woods because I wished to live deliberately, to front only the essential facts of life, and see if I could not learn what it had to teach, and not, when I came to die, discover that I had not lived.", "attr": "Henry David Thoreau, Walden, or Life in the Woods (1854)"}}, {"id": "p4-033", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The American Renaissance in literature", "topic_zh": "美国文艺复兴", "year": null, "year_text": "1850s: The Scarlet Letter (1850), Moby Dick (1851), Leaves of Grass (1855)", "who": ["Nathaniel Hawthorne", "Herman Melville", "Walt Whitman"], "who_zh": ["纳撒尼尔·霍桑", "赫尔曼·梅尔维尔", "沃尔特·惠特曼"], "what_en": "Hawthorne's The Scarlet Letter (1850) explored excessive individualism through Hester Prynne and Arthur Dimmesdale, whose adultery brings guilt rather than liberation; Melville's Moby Dick (1851) made Captain Ahab's obsessive whale hunt a scathing critique of transcendentalism; Whitman's Leaves of Grass (1855) celebrated the individual — \"I celebrate myself, and sing myself\" — giving collective democracy a sacred character.", "what_zh": "霍桑《红字》（1850）通过海丝特·白兰与丁梅斯代尔的通奸（带来罪疚而非解放）探讨过度个人主义；梅尔维尔《白鲸》（1851）以亚哈船长执念般的捕鲸成为对超验主义的尖刻批判；惠特曼《草叶集》（1855）歌颂个人——\"我歌唱我自己\"——赋予集体民主以神圣色彩。", "cause_en": "Emerson's writings influenced all three authors, but Hawthorne and Melville held more pessimistic worldviews, warning that unfettered egoism could destroy individuals and those around them.", "cause_zh": "三位作家都受爱默生影响，但霍桑与梅尔维尔的世界观更为悲观，警告不受约束的自我主义会毁灭个人及其周围的人。", "sig_en": "A mid-nineteenth-century flourishing of American literature and philosophy that displayed both the promise of individualism and its dark limits; Moby Dick flopped commercially because middle-class readers rejected its vision of individualism gone mad.", "sig_zh": "十九世纪中期美国文学与哲学的繁荣，既展现了个人主义的前景，也展现了它的黑暗极限；《白鲸》商业失败，正是因为中产阶级读者拒绝接受\"发疯的个人主义\"。", "exp_en": "The American Renaissance tested Emerson's creed in fiction: Whitman sanctified it, Hawthorne and Melville warned against it.", "exp_zh": "美国文艺复兴在小说中检验了爱默生的信条：惠特曼将其神圣化，霍桑与梅尔维尔则发出警告。", "page": 348, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2980", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.348"}}, {"id": "p4-034", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Utopian communities: Fourierism and Oneida perfectionism", "topic_zh": "乌托邦社区：傅立叶主义与奥奈达完美主义", "year": null, "year_text": "1840s (nearly 100 Fourierist communities; Oneida founded 1848)", "who": ["Charles Fourier", "Albert Brisbane", "John Humphrey Noyes"], "who_zh": ["夏尔·傅立叶", "阿尔伯特·布里斯班", "约翰·汉弗莱·诺伊斯"], "what_en": "During the 1840s Fourierists started nearly one hundred cooperative communities (phalanxes) in western New York and the Midwest, most collapsing quickly over work and social disputes; John Humphrey Noyes's perfectionist community moved to Oneida, New York, in 1848, practicing \"complex marriage,\" in which all members were married to one another.", "what_zh": "19世纪40年代，傅立叶主义者在纽约西部和中西部建立了近百个合作社区（法郎吉），多数因劳作与社会政策之争迅速瓦解；约翰·汉弗莱·诺伊斯的完美主义社区于1848年迁至纽约州奥奈达，实行\"复杂婚姻\"——所有成员互为夫妻。", "cause_en": "Farmers and artisans sought refuge from the depression of 1837–1843 and yearned for economic stability and communal solidarity; religious idealists sought new rules for property, marriage, and gender roles through common ownership of property (socialism).", "cause_zh": "农民与工匠为躲避1837–1843年经济萧条、渴望经济稳定与社区团结而聚集；宗教理想主义者则试图通过财产公有（社会主义）建立关于财产、婚姻与性别的新规则。", "sig_en": "Fourierism's rapid decline revealed how hard it was to sustain a utopia without a charismatic leader or religious vision; the utopians' radical questioning of sexual norms and capitalist values stood as countercultural blueprints of a more egalitarian social and economic order.", "sig_zh": "傅立叶主义的迅速衰落表明，没有超凡领袖或宗教愿景的乌托邦难以为继；乌托邦主义者对性规范与资本主义价值观的激进质疑，成为更平等社会经济秩序的反文化蓝图。", "exp_en": "Secular utopias failed fast; only charismatic, religiously grounded experiments like Oneida — or the Mormons — endured.", "exp_zh": "世俗乌托邦迅速失败；只有奥奈达、摩门教这样有超凡领袖与宗教根基的实验才得以存续。", "page": 351, "src": {"text": "Exclusiveness, jealousy, quarreling have no place at the marriage supper of the Lamb.", "attr": "John Humphrey Noyes"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2989", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.351"}}, {"id": "p4-035", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Joseph Smith and the Book of Mormon", "topic_zh": "约瑟夫·史密斯与《摩门经》", "year": 1830, "year_text": "1830 (Book of Mormon published); Smith murdered at Carthage 1844", "who": ["Joseph Smith Jr."], "who_zh": ["小约瑟夫·史密斯"], "what_en": "In 1830 Smith published The Book of Mormon, claiming to have translated it from ancient hieroglyphics on gold plates shown to him by an angel named Moroni; he organized the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, reviving patriarchal authority and preaching moral perfection. In 1844 an anti-Mormon mob murdered Smith and his brother in the Carthage, Illinois, jail.", "what_zh": "1830年史密斯出版《摩门经》，声称译自天使摩罗乃向他展示的金页片上的古代象形文字；他创立了耶稣基督后期圣徒教会，重振父权权威，宣扬道德完美。1844年，反摩门暴徒在伊利诺伊州卡太基监狱杀害了史密斯及其兄弟。", "cause_en": "Religious ferment among families of Puritan descent along the Erie Canal, heirs to a tradition of wonders and visions; Smith believed God had singled him out for a special revelation and saw himself as a prophet in a sinful, excessively individualistic society.", "cause_zh": "伊利诺伊运河沿岸清教后裔家庭中的宗教狂热（承袭神迹异象传统）；史密斯相信上帝拣选他接受特殊启示，自视为罪恶而过度个人主义社会中的先知。", "sig_en": "Because of their cohesiveness, authoritarian leadership, and size, the Mormons provoked more animosity than the radical utopians — and became the most successful communal experiment of the era.", "sig_zh": "摩门教徒因其凝聚力、权威型领导与规模，招致的敌意超过激进乌托邦主义者，也成为本时代最成功的社区实验。", "exp_en": "Mormonism fused conservative social doctrine with communal discipline: patriarchal, authoritarian, and built to last.", "exp_zh": "摩门教把保守的社会教义与社区纪律结合起来：父权制、权威主义，且为长久而建。", "page": 352, "src": {"text": "A pillar of light above the brightness of the sun at noonday came down from above and rested upon me and I was filled with the spirit of God.", "attr": "Joseph Smith Jr."}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2991", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.352"}}, {"id": "p4-036", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Brigham Young, the Mormon trek to Salt Lake, and the \"Mormon War\"", "topic_zh": "杨百翰、摩门教徒西迁盐湖与\"摩门战争\"", "year": 1846, "year_text": "1846 (Mormon trek begins); 1858 (Mormon War ends)", "who": ["Brigham Young", "James Buchanan"], "who_zh": ["杨百翰", "詹姆斯·布坎南"], "what_en": "Beginning in 1846, about 6,500 Mormons led by Brigham Young fled the United States and settled the Great Salt Lake Valley in present-day Utah, spreading agricultural communities along the Wasatch Range through cooperative labor and communal irrigation. When Young and the Utah legislature vowed to resist federal laws, President Buchanan sent an army; the \"Mormon War\" ended quietly in June 1858 after Buchanan pardoned Utahns who acknowledged federal authority.", "what_zh": "1846年起，约六千五百名摩门教徒在杨百翰率领下逃离美国，定居今犹他州大盐湖谷地，依靠合作劳动与公有灌溉在瓦萨奇山麓建立农业社区。当杨百翰与犹他领地议会公开扬言抵制联邦法律时，布坎南总统派出军队；\"摩门战争\"于1858年6月悄然结束，布坎南赦免了承认联邦权威的犹他居民。", "cause_en": "Constant harassment by anti-Mormons, Smith's murder, and neighbors' resentment of Mormon prosperity, bloc voting, secret rituals, and polygamy (\"plural celestial marriage\"); Young ruled the new Utah Territory (1850) in authoritarian fashion.", "cause_zh": "反摩门势力的持续骚扰、史密斯被杀，以及邻居对摩门教徒的繁荣、整体投票、秘密仪式和一夫多妻制（\"多元天国婚姻\"）的怨恨；杨百翰以权威方式统治1850年成立的犹他领地。", "sig_en": "The Salt Lake Mormons succeeded where other experiments failed by combining strict religious control with private property and enterprise; fearing that forced abolition of polygamy would set a precedent for ending slavery, Buchanan backed down, and Utah later won statehood (1896) by banning polygamy.", "sig_zh": "盐湖摩门教徒把严格的宗教控制与私有财产、个人创业结合起来，在其他实验失败之处取得成功；布坎南担心强制废除一夫多妻制会成为废奴的先例而让步，犹他后来以禁止一夫多妻制换取建州（1896年）。", "exp_en": "The Mormon trek shows the era's paradox: a communal movement that survived by endorsing the market society it fled.", "exp_zh": "摩门西迁展现了时代的悖论：一个社区运动靠拥抱它所逃离的市场社会而存续下来。", "page": 353, "img": {"file": "img:f1_2994", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.353"}}, {"id": "p4-037", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Minstrelsy", "topic_zh": "黑人歌舞剧", "year": null, "year_text": "1830s (minstrelsy begins); hundreds of troupes by the 1840s", "who": ["John Dartmouth Rice"], "who_zh": ["约翰·达特茅斯·赖斯"], "what_en": "Beginning around 1830, white actors in blackface presented minstrel shows combining racist caricature and social criticism; John Dartmouth Rice's \"Jim Crow\" blended a shuffle-dance-and-jump with lyrics in \"Negro dialect,\" and by the 1840s hundreds of troupes — including some black entertainers — toured the country.", "what_zh": "约1830年起，白人演员涂黑脸表演黑人歌舞剧，把种族主义丑化表演与社会批评结合起来；约翰·达特茅斯·赖斯的\"吉姆·克劳\"把怪异的拖步跳舞与\"黑人方言\"歌词结合；到1840年代已有数百个剧团在全国巡演。", "cause_en": "A new urban popular culture gave New York workingmen cheap theatrical entertainment; minstrels portrayed blacks as lazy, sensual, and irresponsible while also mocking Irish and German immigrants, women's rights demands, and upper-class arrogance.", "cause_zh": "新兴的城市大众文化为纽约工人提供廉价戏剧娱乐；歌舞剧把黑人描绘成懒惰、纵欲、不负责任，同时也嘲讽爱尔兰与德国移民、妇女权利诉求和上层男性的傲慢。", "sig_en": "By caricaturing blacks, the minstrels declared the importance of being white and spread racist sentiments among Irish and German immigrants; such racist caricatures influenced white views of African Americans well into the twentieth century.", "sig_zh": "通过丑化黑人，歌舞剧宣示了\"白人身份\"的重要性，并把种族主义情绪传播到爱尔兰与德国移民中；这类种族主义丑化表演影响了白人对非裔美国人的看法，一直延续到二十世纪。", "exp_en": "Minstrelsy was the racist underside of the new urban culture: entertainment that bonded white workers through shared contempt for blacks.", "exp_zh": "黑人歌舞剧是新兴城市文化的种族主义暗面：以对黑人的共同蔑视来团结白人工人的娱乐。", "page": 356}, {"id": "p4-038", "period": 4, "topic_en": "David Walker's Appeal and Nat Turner's Rebellion", "topic_zh": "戴维·沃克的《呼吁书》与纳特·特纳起义", "year": 1831, "year_text": "1829 (Walker's Appeal); 1831 (Turner's rebellion)", "who": ["David Walker", "Nat Turner"], "who_zh": ["戴维·沃克", "纳特·特纳"], "what_en": "In 1829 the free black Bostonian David Walker published An Appeal . . . to the Colored Citizens of the World, ridiculing slaveholders' religious pretensions and justifying slave rebellion. In August 1831 the slave Nat Turner, taking a solar eclipse as an omen, led a revolt in Southampton County, Virginia, killing at least 55 white men, women, and children; he mustered only 60 men, was captured, and hanged — \"Was not Christ crucified?\"", "what_zh": "1829年，波士顿自由黑人戴维·沃克发表《告世界有色公民书》，嘲讽奴隶主的宗教伪善，为奴隶反抗辩护。1831年8月，奴隶纳特·特纳以日食为凶兆，在弗吉尼亚州南安普敦县发动起义，杀死至少55名白人男女老幼；他只聚集到60人，被捕后绞死——\"基督不也被钉在十字架上吗？\"", "cause_en": "Violent white attacks on black communities in northern cities and whites' refusal to accept African Americans as social equals; Walker warned of revolt in biblical language, and Turner acted on a religious vision that Christ had laid down the yoke and he should \"fight against the Serpent.\"", "cause_zh": "北方城市白人对黑人社区的暴力袭击，以及白人拒绝把非裔美国人当作社会平等成员；沃克用圣经语言警告奴隶起义，特纳则依据宗教异象（基督已放下轭，他应\"与蛇争战\"）采取行动。", "sig_en": "Deeply shaken, the Virginia assembly debated gradual emancipation and colonization, but the bill failed 73 to 58 — ending forever the possibility that planters would voluntarily end slavery; instead the South toughened slave codes, limited black movement, and banned teaching slaves to read.", "sig_zh": "深受震动的弗吉尼亚议会辩论渐进解放与殖民方案，但法案以73比58被否决——种植园主自愿废奴的可能性永远消失；南方转而收紧奴隶法典、限制黑人流动、禁止教奴隶识字。", "exp_en": "Walker supplied the words and Turner the deed of black revolutionary resistance; together they closed the door on voluntary Southern emancipation.", "exp_zh": "沃克提供了黑人革命反抗的言辞，特纳提供了行动；两人一起关上了南方自愿废奴的大门。", "page": 360, "src": {"text": "We must and shall be free.... And woe, woe, will be it to you if we have to obtain our freedom by fighting.", "attr": "David Walker, An Appeal . . . to the Colored Citizens of the World (1829)"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3013", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.360"}}, {"id": "p4-039", "period": 4, "topic_en": "William Lloyd Garrison, The Liberator, and the American Anti-Slavery Society", "topic_zh": "威廉·劳埃德·加里森、《解放者报》与美国反奴隶制协会", "year": 1831, "year_text": "1831 (The Liberator founded); 1833 (American Anti-Slavery Society)", "who": ["William Lloyd Garrison", "Theodore Weld", "Arthur Tappan", "Lewis Tappan"], "who_zh": ["威廉·劳埃德·加里森", "西奥多·韦尔德", "阿瑟·塔潘", "刘易斯·塔潘"], "what_en": "In 1831 Garrison started the Boston weekly The Liberator (1831–1865), demanding immediate abolition without compensation to slaveholders. In 1833 he, Theodore Weld, and sixty other black and white abolitionists founded the American Anti-Slavery Society, financed by New York silk merchants Arthur and Lewis Tappan.", "what_zh": "1831年加里森在波士顿创办周报《解放者报》（1831–1865），要求立即废奴、不给奴隶主任何补偿。1833年，他与西奥多·韦尔德及另外六十名黑白废奴主义者创立美国反奴隶制协会，由纽约丝绸商阿瑟·塔潘与刘易斯·塔潘资助。", "cause_en": "Drawing on Second Great Awakening religious enthusiasm, Garrison rejected gradualism — influenced by Elizabeth Heyrick's Immediate, Not Gradual Abolition (1824) — condemned slavery as a sin, and assailed the Constitution as \"a covenant with death and an agreement with Hell\" for accepting bondage.", "cause_zh": "加里森汲取第二次大觉醒的宗教热情，拒绝渐进主义（受伊丽莎白·海里克《立即而非渐进废奴》1824年小册子影响），谴责奴隶制为罪恶，并抨击宪法因默许奴役而是\"与死亡立约、与地狱结盟\"。", "sig_en": "Garrisonian abolitionism raised the antislavery banner to new heights with a three-pronged attack — moral suasion, aiding fugitives, and political petitions — but provoked mobs, a $5,000 Georgia bounty on Garrison, and an 1840 movement split over women's rights.", "sig_zh": "加里森式废奴主义以三管齐下（道德感召、援助逃奴、政治请愿）把反奴旗帜举到新高度，但也招致暴徒袭击、佐治亚州悬赏五千美元抓捕加里森，以及1840年因妇女权利问题导致的运动分裂。", "why_term": "immediate abolition", "why_term_q": "加里森要求的废奴方式（不补偿奴隶主）的关键词是 ______。", "exp_en": "Garrison made abolitionism uncompromising: no compensation, no gradualism, no sacred Constitution — and the nation could not ignore him.", "exp_zh": "加里森让废奴主义变得毫不妥协：不补偿、不渐进、宪法也不神圣——全国无法再忽视他。", "page": 362, "src": {"text": "I will not retreat a single inch, and I will be heard.", "attr": "William Lloyd Garrison"}}, {"id": "p4-040", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The Underground Railroad", "topic_zh": "地下铁路", "year": null, "year_text": "1830s–1850s", "who": ["Harriet Tubman", "Frederick Douglass"], "who_zh": ["哈丽雅特·塔布曼", "弗雷德里克·道格拉斯"], "what_en": "The Underground Railroad was an informal network of whites and free blacks in Richmond, Charleston, and other southern towns that assisted fugitives; Harriet Tubman repeatedly risked re-enslavement by returning to the South to lead others out, and about one thousand African Americans reached freedom in the North each year.", "what_zh": "地下铁路是由里士满、查尔斯顿等南方城镇的白人与自由黑人组成的非正式网络，协助逃亡奴隶；哈丽雅特·塔布曼冒着被重新奴役的危险多次返回南方带人逃出，每年约有一千名非裔美国人经此抵达北方获得自由。", "cause_en": "As the second prong of the abolitionists' attack, they provided lodging and jobs for escaped blacks in free states; the Fugitive Slave Law (1793) let owners seize suspected runaways, forcing abolitionists to spirit captives to Canada.", "cause_zh": "作为废奴主义者三管齐下中的第二策，他们在自由州为逃奴提供食宿与工作；1793年《逃奴法》允许奴隶主抓捕疑似逃奴，迫使废奴主义者把获救者转移到加拿大。", "sig_en": "The Railroad drew free blacks and white abolitionists into direct, illegal action against slavery, escalating sectional conflict over fugitive slaves and making the South demand ever harsher enforcement.", "sig_zh": "地下铁路把自由黑人与白人废奴主义者卷入直接的非法反奴行动，加剧了围绕逃奴的 sectional（地区）冲突，促使南方要求更严厉的执法。", "exp_en": "A practical, dangerous expression of abolitionist moral urgency — freedom delivered one fugitive at a time.", "exp_zh": "废奴主义道德紧迫感的实际而危险的表达——一次解救一名逃奴的自由之路。", "page": 362, "src": {"text": "I should fight for . . . liberty as long as my strength lasted", "attr": "Harriet Tubman"}}, {"id": "p4-041", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The great postal campaign and antiabolitionist riots", "topic_zh": "邮政大宣传运动与反废奴暴乱", "year": 1835, "year_text": "1835 (great postal campaign launched)", "who": ["American Anti-Slavery Society", "Elijah P. Lovejoy", "Andrew Jackson"], "who_zh": ["美国反奴隶制协会", "以利亚·P·洛夫乔伊", "安德鲁·杰克逊"], "what_en": "In 1835 the American Anti-Slavery Society used new steam-powered presses to print a million pamphlets and flood the nation, including the South, with antislavery literature; the campaign sparked antiabolitionist riots — a Charleston mob attacked the post office, \"gentlemen of property and standing\" broke up an 1835 Utica convention, and an 1837 Alton, Illinois, mob killed abolitionist editor Elijah P. Lovejoy.", "what_zh": "1835年，美国反奴隶制协会利用新型蒸汽印刷机印制一百万份小册子，向全国（含南方）倾泻反奴文献；运动引发反废奴暴乱——查尔斯顿暴徒袭击邮局、\"有产有身份的绅士\"捣毁1835年尤蒂卡大会、1837年伊利诺伊州奥尔顿暴徒杀害废奴报纸编辑以利亚·P·洛夫乔伊。", "cause_en": "Abolitionists turned to mass communication to win religious Americans; slavery's defenders — ministers, merchants tied to the cotton trade, northern wage earners, and whites fearing \"amalgamation\" — warned that agitation would embitter one section against the other and assault property rights.", "cause_zh": "废奴主义者转向大众传播以争取信教的美国人；奴隶制的捍卫者——牧师、与棉花贸易相关的商人、北方雇工以及恐惧\"种族混合\"的白人——警告这种煽动会使地区对立、冲击财产权。", "sig_en": "The campaign revealed the depth of racial prejudice and heightened race consciousness nationwide; after 1835 southern postmasters simply refused to deliver suspected abolitionist mail, and President Jackson asked Congress to restrict abolitionist use of the mails.", "sig_zh": "运动揭示了种族偏见的深度，并在全国范围内强化了种族意识；1835年后南方邮局长干脆拒投疑似废奴邮件，杰克逊总统要求国会限制废奴主义者使用邮政。", "exp_en": "The postal campaign turned abolitionism from pamphlets into a national crisis — and proved that mass media could terrify a slaveholding republic.", "exp_zh": "邮政运动把废奴主义从小册子变成全国性危机——证明大众传媒足以让一个蓄奴共和国恐惧。", "page": 362}, {"id": "p4-042", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The gag rule", "topic_zh": "缄口规则", "year": 1836, "year_text": "1836 (adopted by the House); in force until 1844", "who": ["House of Representatives"], "who_zh": ["众议院"], "what_en": "In 1836 the House of Representatives adopted the so-called gag rule, an informal agreement under which the House automatically tabled antislavery petitions — the American Anti-Slavery Society had sent nearly 500,000 signatures between 1835 and 1838 — keeping slavery off the congressional stage until 1844.", "what_zh": "1836年众议院通过所谓缄口规则这一非正式协议，自动搁置所有反奴请愿书（美国反奴隶制协会在1835至1838年间寄出近五十万个签名），使奴隶制议题在国会舞台上消失，直到1844年。", "cause_en": "Congress refused President Jackson's 1835 request to restrict abolitionist use of the mails, but lawmakers eager to avoid sectional conflict devised the gag rule to table petitions without discussion.", "cause_zh": "国会拒绝了杰克逊总统1835年限制废奴主义者使用邮政的要求，但急于回避地区冲突的议员们设计出缄口规则，不经讨论即搁置请愿书。", "sig_en": "The rule showed how abolitionist pressure drove the federal government to suppress debate itself, fueling Northern outrage and pushing antislavery energy toward independent political action.", "sig_zh": "该规则表明废奴压力迫使联邦政府压制辩论本身，激起北方义愤，并把反奴能量推向独立的政治行动。", "exp_en": "Congress's attempt to silence slavery made the silence itself the scandal.", "exp_zh": "国会试图让奴隶制噤声，结果噤声本身成了丑闻。", "page": 365, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3030", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.365"}}, {"id": "p4-043", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The Liberty Party and James G. Birney", "topic_zh": "自由党与詹姆斯·G·伯尼", "year": 1840, "year_text": "1840 (Liberty Party nominates Birney for president)", "who": ["James G. Birney"], "who_zh": ["詹姆斯·G·伯尼"], "what_en": "In 1840 Garrison's opponents in the abolitionist split founded the American and Foreign Anti-Slavery Society, turned to politics, and organized the Liberty Party — the first antislavery political party — nominating former Alabama slave owner James G. Birney for president; the party argued the Constitution did not recognize slavery, but Birney won few votes.", "what_zh": "1840年，加里森的反对者在废奴运动分裂后创立美国与外国反奴隶制协会，转向政治，组建了第一个反奴政党——自由党，提名前阿拉巴马奴隶主詹姆斯·G·伯尼为总统候选人；该党主张宪法并不承认奴隶制，但伯尼得票寥寥。", "cause_en": "In 1840 Garrison's demand that the American Anti-Slavery Society support women's rights split the movement; his opponents, who rejected women's public roles, channeled their energy into electoral politics instead.", "cause_zh": "1840年加里森要求美国反奴隶制协会支持妇女权利，导致运动分裂；反对他的人拒绝妇女的公共角色，转而把精力投入选举政治。", "sig_en": "The first attempt at antislavery electoral politics; though Birney's poor showing made political abolitionism's future appear dim, it foreshadowed the Free Soil and Republican parties.", "sig_zh": "反奴选举政治的首次尝试；尽管伯尼的惨淡得票使政治废奴主义前途看似黯淡，它却预示了自由土地党与共和党的到来。", "exp_en": "The Liberty Party marks the moment abolitionism split into moral suasion (Garrison) and ballot-box politics.", "exp_zh": "自由党标志着废奴主义分裂为道德感召派（加里森）与选票政治派的时刻。", "page": 366, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3032", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.366"}}, {"id": "p4-044", "period": 4, "topic_en": "The women's rights movement: Fuller, the Grimke sisters, and the Seneca Falls Convention", "topic_zh": "妇女权利运动：富勒、格里姆克姐妹与塞内卡福尔斯会议", "year": 1848, "year_text": "1848 (Seneca Falls Convention); also 1837 (Grimke defense), 1844 (Fuller), 1860 (NY property law)", "who": ["Margaret Fuller", "Sarah Grimke", "Angelina Grimke", "Elizabeth Cady Stanton", "Lucretia Mott", "Susan B. Anthony"], "who_zh": ["玛格丽特·富勒", "萨拉·格里姆克", "安吉莉娜·格里姆克", "伊丽莎白·卡迪·斯坦顿", "卢克丽霞·莫特", "苏珊·B·安东尼"], "what_en": "Margaret Fuller's Woman in the Nineteenth Century (1844) demanded women's full intellectual and social independence; after a Congregationalist Pastoral Letter condemned their activism in 1837, Sarah and Angelina Grimke defended women's public roles; Stanton and Mott organized the Seneca Falls Convention (1848), whose Declaration of Sentiments proclaimed \"All men and women are created equal\"; Susan B. Anthony's lobbying then secured an 1860 New York law giving women control of their own wages and property.", "what_zh": "玛格丽特·富勒《十九世纪的妇女》（1844）要求妇女获得完全的心智与社会独立；1837年公理会《牧函》谴责她们的公共活动后，萨拉与安吉莉娜·格里姆克为妇女的公共角色辩护；斯坦顿与莫特组织塞内卡福尔斯会议（1848），其《情感宣言》宣布\"男女皆生而平等\"；苏珊·B·安东尼的游说随后促成1860年纽约州法律，赋予妇女支配自己工资与财产的权利。", "cause_en": "Abolitionist women — the Grimkes, Stanton, Mott — began as antislavery advocates but, denied lecture platforms by male abolitionists and clergy, saw that both enslaved blacks and married women were \"owned\" by men; Fuller applied transcendental individualism to women.", "cause_zh": "格里姆克姐妹、斯坦顿、莫特等人起初是废奴倡导者，但被男性废奴主义者与牧师剥夺讲台后，认识到被奴役的黑人与已婚妇女同样\"属于\"男人；富勒则把超验主义的个人主义应用于妇女。", "sig_en": "Seneca Falls repudiated both the natural inferiority of women and the ideology of separate spheres, launching a sustained campaign for married women's property rights, custody rights, and suffrage — \"the corner-stone of this enterprise.\"", "sig_zh": "塞内卡福尔斯会议否定了妇女天生低劣的观念与\"分开领域\"意识形态，发起了争取已婚妇女财产权、监护权与选举权的持久运动——\"此事业的基石\"。", "why_term": "separate spheres", "why_term_q": "塞内卡福尔斯会议否定的、主张妇女只属家庭领域的意识形态（关键词）是 ______。", "exp_en": "The women's rights movement grew directly out of abolitionism: the same logic that condemned owning people condemned owning wives.", "exp_zh": "妇女权利运动直接生长于废奴主义：谴责\"拥有他人\"的逻辑同样谴责\"拥有妻子\"。", "page": 371, "src": {"text": "All men and women are created equal", "attr": "Declaration of Sentiments, Seneca Falls Convention (1848)"}, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3045", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.371"}}, {"id": "p4-045", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Dorothea Dix and asylum reform", "topic_zh": "多萝西娅·迪克斯与精神病院改革", "year": 1841, "year_text": "1841 (Dix begins her campaign for the mentally ill)", "who": ["Dorothea Dix"], "who_zh": ["多萝西娅·迪克斯"], "what_en": "In 1841 Dix discovered insane women jailed alongside male criminals and persuaded Massachusetts lawmakers to enlarge the state hospital to house indigent mental patients; exhilarated, she began a national movement, and by 1854 had traveled more than 30,000 miles, visiting eighteen state penitentiaries, three hundred county jails, and over five hundred almshouses and hospitals.", "what_zh": "1841年迪克斯发现精神失常的妇女与男性罪犯关押在一起，说服马萨诸塞州议会扩建州立医院以收容贫困精神病人；深受鼓舞的她发起全国性运动，到1854年已跋涉三万余英里，走访十八所州立监狱、三百所县监狱和五百多所济贫院与医院。", "cause_en": "Emotionally abused as a child by an alcoholic father, Dix grew into a compassionate woman with a strong sense of moral purpose; her Massachusetts success convinced her that investigation and publicity could move legislatures.", "cause_zh": "童年遭酗酒父亲情感虐待的迪克斯成长为富有同情心、道德使命感强烈的女性；她在马萨诸塞州的成功使她相信调查与舆论能够推动立法机构行动。", "sig_en": "Dix's reports and agitation prompted many states to establish public asylums for the mentally ill and improve prisons and hospitals, making her the model of women's institutional reform.", "sig_zh": "迪克斯的报告与奔走促使许多州建立公立精神病院、改善监狱与医院，使她成为妇女制度改革的典范。", "exp_en": "Dix turned private compassion into public policy: one woman's inspection tour rebuilt how America treated the mentally ill.", "exp_zh": "迪克斯把私人同情变成公共政策：一位女性的巡视之旅重塑了美国对待精神病人的方式。", "page": 367}, {"id": "p4-046", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Cotton is King", "topic_zh": "“棉花为王”与棉花经济", "year": 1840, "year_text": "By 1840", "who": ["Southern Cultivator"], "who_zh": ["《南方耕耘者》杂志"], "what_en": "By 1840 the South annually produced and exported 1.5 million bales of raw cotton — over two-thirds of the world's supply — and its economy was larger and richer than that of most nations. \"Cotton is King,\" boasted the Southern Cultivator.", "what_zh": "到1840年，南方每年生产并出口150万包原棉——超过世界供应量的三分之二——其经济规模超过多数国家。《南方耕耘者》杂志夸耀道：“棉花为王。”", "cause_en": "The Market Revolution and westward expansion opened millions of acres of fertile land in Alabama, Mississippi, Louisiana, and Texas, while the domestic slave trade supplied the forced labor to plant it with cotton.", "cause_zh": "市场革命与西进运动在阿拉巴马、密西西比、路易斯安那和得克萨斯开辟了数百万英亩肥沃土地，国内奴隶贸易则提供了种植棉花的强制劳力。", "sig_en": "Cotton made slavery enormously profitable and tied the South's prosperity to the expansion of plantation agriculture, intensifying the demand for enslaved labor and western land.", "sig_zh": "棉花使奴隶制获利丰厚，将南方的繁荣与种植园农业扩张绑定，加剧了对奴隶劳力和西部土地的需求。", "why_term": "Cotton is King", "why_term_q": "《南方耕耘者》杂志用来形容棉花经济的口号是 ______。", "exp_en": "By 1840 the South's 1.5-million-bale cotton output made 'Cotton is King' a boast and an economic reality: cotton's profits financed the westward plantation frontier and deepened the South's dependence on slavery.", "exp_zh": "到1840年南方年150万包的棉花产量使“棉花为王”既是夸耀也是经济现实：棉花利润资助了种植园西进边疆，加深了南方对奴隶制的依赖。", "page": 376}, {"id": "p4-047", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Domestic Slave Trade (Coastal Trade and Inland System)", "topic_zh": "国内奴隶贸易（沿海贸易与内陆系统）", "year": null, "year_text": "1800–1860", "who": ["slave traders", "Upper South planters"], "who_zh": ["奴隶贩子", "上南方种植园主"], "what_en": "Between 1790 and 1860 more than 1 million enslaved African Americans were forcibly moved from the Upper South to the Deep South. The coastal trade shipped slaves through port cities like Baltimore and Richmond to the New Orleans market and Louisiana sugar plantations, while the less visible inland system marched slaves in coffles to Alabama, Mississippi, Missouri, Arkansas, and Texas. About 60 percent of the 1 million migrants were \"sold south\" through traders; the rest were transferred by migrating planters.", "what_zh": "1790–1860年间，超过100万被奴役的非裔被强制从上南方迁往深南方。沿海贸易经巴尔的摩、里富蒙德等港口城市将奴隶运往新奥尔良市场和路易斯安那甘蔗种植园；更隐蔽的内陆系统则用锁链队伍将奴隶押往阿拉巴马、密西西比、密苏里、阿肯色和得克萨斯。100万移民中约60%是经贩子“被卖往南方”的，其余为迁移种植园主的转移。", "cause_en": "The cotton boom created an insatiable demand for labor in the Gulf states while natural increase produced a surplus of enslaved workers on Chesapeake and Carolina plantations, and Congress had ended the Atlantic slave trade in 1807.", "cause_zh": "棉花热使墨西哥湾各州对劳力的需求无止境，而切萨皮克和卡罗来纳种植园因自然增长出现了奴隶剩余；国会于1807年终止了大西洋奴隶贸易。", "sig_en": "The trade transplanted a majority of African Americans to the Deep South, enriched both migrating cotton planters and Upper South slave sellers, and shattered black families and communities.", "sig_zh": "该贸易使多数非裔美国人被移植到深南方，既富了西迁的棉花种植园主，也富了出售奴隶的上南方奴隶主，同时摧毁了黑人家庭和社区。", "exp_en": "After the Atlantic trade ended, a domestic trade in over a million slaves fueled the Cotton South: a visible coastal trade fed Louisiana sugar, while a larger inland system in coffles fed the cotton belt — both devastating black family life.", "exp_zh": "大西洋贸易终止后，超过100万奴隶的国内贸易驱动了棉花南方：显眼的沿海贸易供应路易斯安那甘蔗业，更庞大的内陆系统以锁链队伍供应棉花带——两者都重创黑人家庭生活。", "page": 380}, {"id": "p4-048", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Chattel Principle", "topic_zh": "动产原则", "year": null, "year_text": "antebellum era", "who": ["James W. C. Pennington", "Henry Clay"], "who_zh": ["詹姆斯·W.C.·彭宁顿", "亨利·克莱"], "what_en": "Under the chattel principle, enslaved African Americans were the movable personal property of the whites who owned them. \"The being of slavery, its soul and its body, lives and moves in the chattel principle, the property principle, the bill of sale principle,\" declared former slave James W. C. Pennington.", "what_zh": "根据动产原则，被奴役的非裔是奴隶主的可移动个人财产。前奴隶詹姆斯·W.C.·彭宁顿宣称：“奴隶制的本质、灵魂与躯体，都存在并运行于动产原则、财产原则、买卖契约原则之中。”", "cause_en": "Southern law defined slaves as property — \"that is property which the law declares to be property,\" as Henry Clay put it — making slave property, held even by widows and orphans, the foundation of the southern economic system.", "cause_zh": "南方法律把奴隶定义为财产——正如亨利·克莱所言，“法律宣布为财产的东西就是财产”——使寡寘和孤儿也持有的奴隶财产成为整个南方经济体系的根基。", "sig_en": "Because slaves were property, owners could sell them at will, and the threat of sale became a key tool of discipline: \"The Negroes here dread nothing on earth so much as this,\" a Maryland observer noted.", "sig_zh": "既然奴隶是财产，主人可随意出售，出售威胁成为重要的纪律工具：一位马里兰观察者指出，“这里的黑人世上最怕的就是这个。”", "why_term": "chattel principle", "why_term_q": "把奴隶定义为可动产个人财产的法律原则称为 ______。", "src": {"text": "The being of slavery, its soul and its body, lives and moves in the chattel principle, the property principle, the bill of sale principle,", "attr": "former slave James W. C. Pennington"}, "exp_en": "The chattel principle made enslaved people movable property under law, underpinning the southern economy and giving masters the ultimate disciplinary weapon: the threat of sale.", "exp_zh": "动产原则使被奴役者在法律上成为可移动财产，支撑了南方经济，并赋予主人终极的纪律武器：出售威胁。", "page": 381, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3069", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.381"}}, {"id": "p4-049", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Benevolent Masters and Harriet Jacobs", "topic_zh": "“仁慈主人”神话与哈丽雅特·雅各布斯", "year": null, "year_text": "antebellum era", "who": ["Harriet Jacobs"], "who_zh": ["哈丽雅特·雅各布斯"], "what_en": "Many planters considered themselves \"benevolent masters\" committed to the welfare of \"my family, black and white,\" seeing only the slave marriages that endured and ignoring those they had broken. Black abolitionist Harriet Jacobs, in her autobiography Incidents in the Life of a Slave Girl, exposed this paternalist fiction, asking, \"Why does the slave ever love?\" when her partner \"may at any moment be wrenched away by the hand of violence?\"", "what_zh": "许多种植园主自认是致力于“我黑白大家庭”福祉的“仁慈主人”，只看到存续下来的奴隶婚姻，无视自己拆散的那些。黑人废奴主义者哈丽雅特·雅各布斯在自传《女奴生平记》中揭露了这种家长制虚构，质问道：“奴隶为何还要去爱？”——当她的伴侣“随时可能被暴力之手夺走”时。", "cause_en": "Planters who claimed benevolence \"saw\" only the African American marriages that endured and convinced themselves they \"sold south\" only troublemakers with \"little sense of family.\"", "cause_zh": "自称仁慈的种植园主只“看到”存续的黑人婚姻，并说服自己“卖往南方”的只是“家庭观念淡薄”的涌事者。", "sig_en": "Jacobs's testimony punctured the paternalist myth, showing that slavery's violence shadowed even moments of joy and love among the enslaved.", "sig_zh": "雅各布斯的证言戳破了家长制神话，表明奴隶制的暴力甚至笼罩着被奴役者欢乐与爱情的时刻。", "src": {"text": "Why does the slave ever love?", "attr": "Harriet Jacobs, Incidents in the Life of a Slave Girl"}, "exp_en": "While planters posed as benevolent masters of \"my family, black and white,\" Harriet Jacobs's Incidents in the Life of a Slave Girl revealed that the domestic slave trade's destruction of black families made a mockery of that claim.", "exp_zh": "当种植园主扮扮作仁慈的“黑白大家庭”之父时，雅各布斯的《女奴生平记》揭露：国内奴隶贸易对黑人家庭的摧毁让这一说法成为笑柄。", "page": 382, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3072", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.382"}}, {"id": "p4-050", "period": 4, "topic_en": "\"Positive Good\" Argument for Slavery", "topic_zh": "奴隶制“积极善”论", "year": null, "year_text": "1830s–1858", "who": ["James Henry Hammond", "Alexander Stephens"], "who_zh": ["詹姆斯·亨利·哈蒙德", "亚历山大·斯蒂芬斯"], "what_en": "In the 1830s southern apologists abandoned Jefferson's view of slavery as a \"necessary evil\" and argued instead that it was a \"positive good\": it subsidized an elegant lifestyle for a white elite and provided tutelage for supposedly inferior Africans. \"As a race, the African is inferior to the white man,\" declared Alexander Stephens. In his 1858 Senate speech, James Henry Hammond claimed slaves were \"hired for life and well compensated\" while northern wage laborers were \"essentially slaves.\"", "what_zh": "1830年代，南方辩诺士抛弃杰斐逊“必要之恶”的看法，转而主张奴隶制是“积极善”：它供养白人精英的优雅生活，并为所谓劣等的非洲人提供教化。亚历山大·斯蒂芬斯宣称：“作为一个种族，非洲人低于白人。”詹姆斯·亨利·哈蒙德在1858年参议院演说中声称奴隶是“终身雇佣、报酬优厚”，而北方雇佣工人“本质上是奴隶”。", "cause_en": "Mounting abolitionist attacks forced slavery's defenders to produce a moral defense of the institution rather than merely an economic one.", "cause_zh": "日益高涨的废奴主义攻击迫使奴隶制的辩护者为之提供道德辩护，而不仅仅是经济辩护。", "sig_en": "The \"positive good\" defense hardened sectional divisions by presenting slavery as morally superior to northern free labor, making compromise harder.", "sig_zh": "“积极善”辩护把奴隶制描绘成在道德上优于北方自由劳工，加剧了地区对立，使妥协更加困难。", "why_term": "\"positive good\"", "why_term_q": "1830年代南方辩诺士用来为奴隶制辩护的关键词是 ______。", "src": {"text": "In all social systems there must be a class to do the menial duties, to perform the drudgery of life. . . . We use them for our purpose, and call them slaves.", "attr": "Senator James Henry Hammond, speech to the U.S. Senate, March 4, 1858"}, "exp_en": "Rejecting Jefferson's \"necessary evil,\" 1830s apologists recast slavery as a \"positive good\" — a claim Hammond's 1858 mud-sill speech pushed further by calling northern wage workers the real slaves.", "exp_zh": "抛弃杰斐逊的“必要之恶”后，1830年代的辩诺士把奴隶制重塑为“积极善”——哈蒙德5年1858年“泥垣”演说更进一步，称北方雇佣工人才是真正的奴隶。", "page": 386}, {"id": "p4-051", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Republican Aristocracy", "topic_zh": "共和贵族", "year": null, "year_text": "antebellum era", "who": ["James Henry Hammond"], "who_zh": ["詹姆斯·亨利·哈蒙德"], "what_en": "Wealthy southern planters cast themselves as a \"republican aristocracy.\" \"The planters here are essentially what the nobility are in other countries,\" declared James Henry Hammond of South Carolina: they \"stand at the head of society & politics . . . [and form] an aristocracy of talents, of virtue, of generosity and courage.\" Drawing on classical republican theory rooted in Greek and Roman slave societies, they feared federal interference with their slave property and populist politicians who would mobilize poorer whites.", "what_zh": "富裕的南方种植园主把自己塑造成“共和贵族”。南卡罗来纳的詹姆斯·亨利·哈蒙德宣称：“这里的种植园主本质上就是其他国家的贵族”，他们“站在社会与政治的顶端——构成了一个才智、德行、態慨与勇气的贵族”。他们援引根植于希腊罗马奴隶社会的古典共和理论，既怕联邦政府干预其奴隶财产，也怕动员贫穷白人的民粹政客。", "cause_en": "The Old South gentry inherited the manners of the English landed gentry and, after the Revolution of 1776, wrapped them in a republican glaze drawn from classical societies where slavery was part of the natural order.", "cause_zh": "旧南方乡绅继承了英国地主乡绅的风范，1776年革命后又为其披上古典共和理论的外衣——那些古典社会视奴隶制为天经地义。", "sig_en": "This self-image justified planter dominance of southern society and politics and their hostility to northern democracy and universal suffrage.", "sig_zh": "这种自我形象为种植园主主导南方社会政治、敌视北方民主与普选权提供了正当性。", "exp_en": "Old South planters saw themselves as a republican aristocracy — a nobility of talent and virtue — which legitimized their rule and their contempt for democratic politics and universal suffrage.", "exp_zh": "旧南方种植园主自视为才智与德行的共和贵族，这为他们的统治以及对民主政治与普选权的蔑视提供了正当性。", "page": 386}, {"id": "p4-052", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Gang-Labor System and Task System", "topic_zh": "分队劳动制与定额劳动制", "year": null, "year_text": "1820s onward", "who": ["cotton planters", "Carolina rice planters"], "who_zh": ["棉花种植园主", "卡罗来纳稻米种植园主"], "what_en": "During the 1820s profit-seeking cotton planters adopted a rigorous gang-labor system: masters with twenty or more slaves organized disciplined teams, or \"gangs,\" supervised by black drivers and white overseers who worked them at a steady pace clearing, hoeing, and picking cotton. In the Carolina rice country, by contrast, slaves worked by the task — a precisely defined daily job, such as hoeing half an acre — and by finishing early often had the rest of the day for their own fields and profit.", "what_zh": "1820年代，逐利的棉花种植园主采用严苛的分队劳动制：拥有20名以上奴隶的主人把奴隶编成纪律严明的劳动队，由黑人监工和白人工头督督，以稳定节奏开荒、锄草、摘棉。与之相对，卡罗来纳稻米产区的奴隶实行定额制——每天完成精确规定的工作量（如锄半英亩地），提前干完后剩余时间可经营自己的田地获利。", "cause_en": "Cotton's long growing season and surging prices pushed planters to maximize output; slaves in gangs finished tasks in thirty-five minutes that took a white yeoman an hour.", "cause_zh": "棉花漫长的生长季和飙升的价格驱使种植园主最大化产量；分队劳动的奴隶 35分钟就能干完白人自耕农一小时的活。", "sig_en": "Gang labor raised plantation productivity and profits but made cotton slaves' lives far more regimented and grueling than those of task-system rice workers.", "sig_zh": "分队劳动制提高了种植园生产力与利润，但使棉花奴隶的生活远比定额制下的稻米奴隶更受管束、更劳苦。", "exp_en": "The Cotton South's gang-labor system traded workers' autonomy for output, while the Carolina task system left slaves time for their own profit — two labor regimes reflecting different crops and different degrees of planter control.", "exp_zh": "棉花南方的分队劳动制以劳动者的自主换取产量，而卡罗来纳的定额制留给奴隶自己获利的时间——两种劳动制度反映了不同作物与不同程度的主人控制。", "page": 388}, {"id": "p4-053", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Slave Society", "topic_zh": "奴隶社会", "year": null, "year_text": "by 1860", "who": ["white southerners"], "who_zh": ["南方白人"], "what_en": "The antebellum South was a \"slave society\" — that is, a society in which the institution of slavery affected all aspects of life — even though most white southerners did not own slaves: the share of white families holding blacks in bondage steadily fell from 36 percent in 1830 to about 25 percent by 1860.", "what_zh": "战前南方是一个“奴隶社会”——即奴隶制影响生活方方面面的社会——尽管多数南方白人并不拥有奴隶：拥有奴隶的白人家庭比例从1830年的36%持续下降到1860年的约25%。", "cause_en": "The cotton economy concentrated wealth and slaves in fewer hands, increasing inequality even as patrols, militias, and racial privilege bound nonslaveholders to the system.", "cause_zh": "棉花经济使财富和奴隶集中于少数人之手，加剧不平等；同时巡逻队、民兵和种族特权把非奴隶主也绑进这个体系。", "sig_en": "The concept explains why even the nonslaveholding white majority defended slavery: their status, politics, and racial identity were all shaped by it.", "sig_zh": "这一概念解释了为何连占多数的非奴隶主白人也捍卫奴隶制：他们的地位、政治和种族身份都由奴隶制塑造。", "why_term": "slave society", "why_term_q": "教材用来描述奴隶制渗透生活方方面面的南方的关键词是 ______。", "exp_en": "A \"slave society\" is one where slavery shapes every aspect of life — unlike a mere \"society with slaves\" — which is why most nonslaveholding whites still defended the institution.", "exp_zh": "“奴隶社会”指奴隶制塑造生活每一个方面的社会——而非仅仅是“有奴隶的社会”——这就是多数非奴隶主白人仍捍卫奴隶制的原因。", "page": 388}, {"id": "p4-054", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Black Protestantism", "topic_zh": "黑人新教", "year": null, "year_text": "1790s–1840s", "who": ["enslaved African Americans", "black preachers"], "who_zh": ["被奴役的非裔美国人", "黑人传教士"], "what_en": "During the Second Great Awakening (1790s–1840s), enslaved blacks blended African and European traditions into a distinctive black Protestantism: they adapted evangelical doctrines to black needs, ignored teachings on original sin, predestination, and obedience to masters, and worshipped through the African-derived \"ring shout\" and spontaneous spirituals. \"O my Lord delivered Daniel,\" the slaves sang, \"O why not deliver me too?\"", "what_zh": "第二次大觉醒时期（1790–1840年代），被奴役的黑人把非洲与欧洲传统融合成独特的黑人新教：他们按黑人需求改造福音派教义，无视原罪、预定论和服从主人的经文，以源自非洲的“环舞呼喊”和即兴灵歌敬拜。“主啊你拯救了但以理，”奴隶们唱道，“为何不也拯救我？”", "cause_en": "Zealous white and black Protestant preachers carried the evangelical message of emotional conversion, ritual baptism, and communal spirituality to the Cotton South, and black converts made it their own.", "cause_zh": "白人与黑人的热忱新教传教士把情感皈依、洗礼、集体灵性的福音信息带到棉花南方，黑人皈依者又将其改造为自己的信仰。", "sig_en": "Black Protestantism gave enslaved people spiritual autonomy and hope — some envisioned God as the Old Testament warrior who liberated the Jews and would liberate them — sustaining them on the long journey to emancipation and the Promised Land.", "sig_zh": "黑人新教赋予被奴役者精神自主与希望——有人把上帝想像成解放犹太人的旧约战神、终将解放他们——支撑他们走向解放与许诺之地的漫长旅程。", "src": {"text": "\"O my Lord delivered Daniel,\" the slaves sang, \"O why not deliver me too?\"", "attr": "slave spiritual"}, "exp_en": "Black Protestantism fused African expression (ring shout, spirituals) with evangelical Christianity while rejecting doctrines of obedience, becoming a source of spiritual independence and liberation hope.", "exp_zh": "黑人新教把非洲表达形式（环舞呼喊、灵歌）与福音派基督教融合，又拒绝服从主人的教义，成为精神独立与解放希望的源泉。", "page": 395}, {"id": "p4-055", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Texas Revolution and the Alamo", "topic_zh": "得克萨斯革命与阿拉莫", "year": 1836, "year_text": "1835–1836", "who": ["Stephen F. Austin", "Sam Houston", "Antonio López de Santa Anna", "Davy Crockett", "Jim Bowie"], "who_zh": ["斯蒂芬·F.·奥斯汀", "萨姆·休斯顿", "安东尼奥·洛佩斯·德·圣安纳", "戴维·克罗克特", "吉姆·鲍伊"], "what_en": "After Mexico's 1835 centralist constitution nullified Texas's concessions, American settlers split into a \"war party\" led by Sam Houston and a \"peace party\" led by Stephen Austin; the war party's rebellion led to the March 2, 1836 declaration of Texas independence and a constitution legalizing slavery. Santa Anna's army wiped out the Texan garrison defending the Alamo in San Antonio and executed about 350 prisoners at Goliad, but Houston's forces routed Santa Anna at San Jacinto in April 1836, winning de facto independence.", "what_zh": "墨西哥1835年中央集权宪法取消了对得克萨斯的让步后，美国移民分裂为休斯顿领导的“战争派”与奥斯汀领导的“和平派”；战争派发动叛乱，于1836年3月2日宣布得克萨斯独立并通过合法化奴隶制的宪法。圣安纳率军在圣安东尼奥的阿拉莫全歼得克萨斯守军，又在戈利亚德处决约350名战俘，但休斯顿的军队1836年4月在圣哈辛托击溃圣安纳，赢得事实独立。", "cause_en": "By 1835 American settlers outnumbered Mexican residents 27,000 to 3,000 and feared Mexico's central government would end slavery and impose national authority; Austin had won an exemption from the law ending slavery, but Santa Anna nullified it.", "cause_zh": "到1835年美国移民以27000比3000远超墨西哥居民，他们恐惧墨西哥中央政府终结奴隶制并强加全国权威；奥斯汀曾赢得废奴法的豁免，但圣安纳将其作废。", "sig_en": "The revolution extended the plantation-slavery frontier into Texas — by 1835 settlers already held 3,000 slaves — while fears that annexation would spark a war with Mexico and a North-South \"death-struggle\" over slavery's extension led President Van Buren to refuse annexation.", "sig_zh": "这场革命把种植园奴隶制边疆推进到得克萨斯——1835年移民已拥有3000名奴隶——而对并入将引发对墨战争及南北就奴隶制扩张“死斗”的恐惧，使范布伦总统拒绝并入得克萨斯。", "why_term": "Remember the Alamo", "why_term_q": "阿拉莫陷落后，美国报纸号召志愿者时使用的口号是 ______。", "src": {"text": "Remember the Alamo", "attr": "New Orleans and New York newspapers, 1836"}, "exp_en": "The Texas Revolution (1835–1836) grew from American settlers' defense of slavery against Mexico's centralist turn: the Alamo and Goliad became rallying cries, and San Jacinto secured a slaveholding Texas Republic — too explosive for Van Buren to annex.", "exp_zh": "得克萨斯革命（1835–1836）源于美国移民为捍卫奴隶制而反抗墨西哥中央集权：阿拉莫与戈利亚德成为集结号，圣哈辛托确立了一个蓄奴的得克萨斯共和国——对范布伦而言太过敏感，不敢并入。", "page": 391}, {"id": "p4-056", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Secret Ballot in Alabama", "topic_zh": "阿拉巴马的秘密投票", "year": 1819, "year_text": "1819", "who": ["Alabama Constitution of 1819"], "who_zh": ["阿拉巴马州1819年宪法"], "what_en": "The Alabama Constitution of 1819 granted suffrage to all white men and provided for a secret ballot (rather than voice-voting), apportionment of legislative seats based on population, and the election of county supervisors, sheriffs, and clerks of court.", "what_zh": "阿拉巴马州1819年宪法赋予所有白人男子选举权，规定秘密投票（取代口头投票）、按人口分配立法席位，并选举县监事、治安官和法院书记官。", "cause_en": "Unlike the colonial planter-aristocrats, Cotton South elites lived in a republican society with a democratic ethos, so political factions had to compete for the votes of the white majority.", "cause_zh": "与殖民地种植园贵族不同，棉花南方的精英生活在具有民主精神的共和社会中，政治派别必须竞争白人多数的选票。", "sig_en": "Democratic provisions like the secret ballot forced elite politicians to court ordinary white voters, even as slave owners kept a grip on offices — nearly 90 percent of Alabama's legislators owned slaves in the early 1840s.", "sig_zh": "秘密投票等民主条款迫使精英政客讨好普通白人选民，但奴隶主仍掌控官职——1840年代初阿拉巴马还90%的议员拥有奴隶。", "exp_en": "Alabama's 1819 constitution paired universal white manhood suffrage with the secret ballot, forcing planter politicians to win ordinary white votes — though nearly all the winners were still slave owners.", "exp_zh": "阿拉巴马1819年宪法把白人男子普选权与秘密投票结合，迫使种植园政客赢得普通白人选票——尽管胜选者几乎全是奴隶主。", "page": 393, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3097", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.393"}}, {"id": "p4-057", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Alabama Fever", "topic_zh": "阿拉巴马热", "year": null, "year_text": "1810s–1850s", "who": ["James Lide", "Eli Lide"], "who_zh": ["詹姆斯·莱德", "伊莱·莱德"], "what_en": "\"Alabama Fever\" drove thousands of Carolinians and other white planters west to Alabama, Mississippi, Louisiana, and Texas in search of fresh cotton land — men like James Lide, who at sixty-five moved his slaves and family to a plantation near Montgomery, Alabama. In 1854 his son Eli moved on to Texas, saying, \"Something within me whispers onward and onward.\"", "what_zh": "“阿拉巴马热”驱使数千卡罗来纳人和其他白人种植园主西迁阿拉巴马、密西西比、路易斯安那和得克萨斯，寻找新的棉花土地——如65岁高龄仍带着奴隶和家人迁往蒙哥马利附近种植园的詹姆斯·莱德。1854年其子伊莱继续西迁得克萨斯，说道：“我内心有个声音低语着：向前，向前。”", "cause_en": "Exhausted soils in the Old South and soaring cotton prices made fresh western lands irresistible, while federal acquisitions, new state admissions, and Indian removal opened the Southwest.", "cause_zh": "旧南方地力耗竞、棉价飙升使西部新土地极具诱惑，而联邦购地、接纳新州和印第安人迁移政策打开了西南部。", "sig_en": "The migration carried plantation slavery from the Upper South across a 900-mile frontier to Texas, more than doubling the area cultivated by slave labor and raising the number of slave states from eight in 1800 to fifteen by 1850.", "sig_zh": "这次迁移把种植园奴隶制从上南方带过900英里的边疆直至得克萨斯，使奴隶劳力耕种面积翻倍有余，蓄奴州从1800年的8个增至1850年的15个。", "src": {"text": "Something within me whispers onward and onward.", "attr": "Eli Lide, 1854"}, "exp_en": "\"Alabama Fever\" was the cotton-driven westward land rush that transplanted planters, slaves, and slavery itself from the Carolinas to Texas, more than doubling slavery's territory.", "exp_zh": "“阿拉巴马热”是棉花驱动的西进土地热，把种植园主、奴隶和奴隶制本身从卡罗来纳移植到得克萨斯，使奴隶制的领地翻倍有余。", "page": 376}, {"id": "p4-058", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Slave Resistance", "topic_zh": "奴隶的抵抗", "year": null, "year_text": "antebellum era", "who": ["enslaved African Americans", "Gabriel and Martin Prosser", "Nat Turner"], "who_zh": ["被奴役的非裔美国人", "加布里埃尔和马丁·普罗瑟", "纳特·特纳"], "what_en": "Most enslaved people resisted passively — slowing work by feigning illness, losing or breaking tools, and sometimes setting fire to barns, poisoning food, or destroying crops. Only a few, among them Gabriel and Martin Prosser (1800) and Nat Turner (1831), plotted mass uprisings; most recognized that revolt would be futile against numerous, well-armed whites.", "what_zh": "多数被奴役者采取消极抵抗——装病怠工、丢失或损坏工具，有时纵火烧谷仓、投毒或毁坏庄稼。只有少数人策划大规模起义，如加布里埃尔和马丁·普罗瑟（1800年）与纳特·特纳（1831年）；多数人认识到，面对人数众多、武装精良的白人，起义注定徒劳。", "cause_en": "The absolute power of masters, enforced by the whip, left slaves few open options; fear of resistance nevertheless pushed many masters to reduce whipping and offer food and privileges as incentives.", "cause_zh": "主人以鞭子维持的绝对权力使奴隶几乎没有公开反抗的空间；但对抵抗的恐惧也促使许多主人减少鞭打，改用食物和特权作为激励。", "sig_en": "Everyday resistance limited owners' power and forced concessions, while masters' sexual violence against black women — from which \"the law holds . . . no protecting arm,\" as ex-slave Bethany Veney lamented — exposed the system's brutality.", "sig_zh": "日常抵抗限制了主人的权力并迫其让步；而主人对黑人女性的性暴力——前奴隶贝瑟尼·维尼哀叹“法律……不提供任何保护之臂”——暴露了该制度的残暴。", "exp_en": "Facing absolute power, most slaves chose daily, covert resistance — broken tools, slow work, sabotage — which quietly limited masters' control, while organized revolt remained rare (Prosser 1800, Turner 1831).", "exp_zh": "面对绝对权力，多数奴隶选择日常的、隐蔽的抵抗——损坏工具、怠工、破坏——默默限制了主人的控制，而有组织的叛乱则罕见（普罗瑟1800、特纳1831）。", "page": 400, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3120", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.400"}}, {"id": "p4-059", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Slave Families and Community", "topic_zh": "奴隶家庭与社区", "year": null, "year_text": "1800–1860", "who": ["enslaved African Americans"], "who_zh": ["被奴役的非裔美国人"], "what_en": "The domestic slave trade destroyed about one in every four slave marriages and separated almost a third of slave children under fourteen from one or both parents; slave unions had no legal standing — \"slaves have no legal capacity to assent to any contract,\" a Louisiana judge ruled. In response, blacks built fictive kinship ties, choosing older community members as \"aunts\" and \"uncles,\" marking marriages with the West African custom of jumping over a broomstick, and naming children for relatives left behind.", "what_zh": "国内奴隶贸易摧毁了约四分之一的奴隶婚姻，使近三分之一14岁以下奴隶儿童与父母一方或双方分离；奴隶婚姻没有法律效力——路易斯安那法官裁定“奴隶没有同意任何契约的法律能力”。作为回应，黑人建立了拟制亲属关系，认社区年长者为“姑姨叔伯”，以西非跳扫帚习俗举行婚礼，并以留在故乡的亲人之名为孩子命名。", "cause_en": "Because sales focused on young adults and could strike without warning, enslaved people created substitute kin networks to survive the constant threat of separation.", "cause_zh": "由于买卖集中于青壮年且随时可能发生，被奴役者创建了替代性亲属网络，以应对时刻存在的分离威胁。", "sig_en": "Family and church became the core institutions of African American society, providing strength and solace amid slavery's tribulations — 75 percent of slave marriages remained unbroken despite the trade.", "sig_zh": "家庭和教会成为非裔美国人社会的核心制度，在奴隶制的苦难中提供力量与慰藉——尽管有奴隶贸易，75%的奴隶婚姻仍未被拆散。", "exp_en": "The domestic trade broke up black families, but enslaved people answered with fictive kinship, broomstick weddings, and naming practices that preserved family values and community bonds.", "exp_zh": "国内贸易拆散了黑人家庭，但被奴役者以拟制亲属、跳扫帚婚礼和命名习俗作为回应，维系了家庭观念与社区纽带。", "page": 382, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3072", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.382"}}, {"id": "p4-060", "period": 4, "topic_en": "Southern White Social Hierarchy", "topic_zh": "南方白人社会等级", "year": 1860, "year_text": "1860", "who": ["planters", "yeomen", "poor whites"], "who_zh": ["种植园主", "自耕农", "贫穷白人"], "what_en": "In 1860, 395,000 southern families owned slaves in a strict hierarchy: the top fifth (just 5 percent of the white population) owned twenty or more slaves and over half of the enslaved population, with average wealth of $56,000. Below them stood middling planters, smallholding yeomen (who ruled their households with firm patriarchal authority), propertyless tenants and farm laborers (about 40 percent of the white population), and destitute poor whites — yet all ranked above blacks, as Hammond told poor whites, \"In a slave country every freeman is an aristocrat.\"", "what_zh": "1860年，39.5万南方家庭拥有奴隶，形成严格等级：顶层五分之一（仅占白人人口5%）拥有20名以上奴隶和过半被奴役人口，平均财富5.6万美元。其下是中层种植园主、小农场自耕农（以家长权威统治家庭）、无产佃农和雇工（约占白人人口40%），以及赤贫白人——但所有人都高于黑人，正如哈蒙德对贫穷白人所说：“在奴隶国家，每个自由人都是贵族。”", "cause_en": "The cotton economy concentrated land and slaves in fewer hands, bidding up slave prices and blocking white laborers' path to wealth, while planter legislatures refused to tax themselves for public schools.", "cause_zh": "棉花经济使土地和奴隶集中于少数人之手，抬高奴价、堵死了白人劳工的致富之路；种植园主主导的议会还拒绝为公立学校征税。", "sig_en": "Inequality made yeomen politically subordinate — \"thoughtful yeomen understood that the slave-based cotton economy sentenced family farmers to a subordinate place\" — yet racial privilege kept most poor whites loyal to the slave system.", "sig_zh": "不平等使自耕农在政治上从属——“有头脑的自耕农明白，以奴隶制为基础的棉花经济注定了家庭农场的从属地位”——但种族特权使多数贫穷白人仍忠于奴隶制。", "src": {"text": "In a slave country every freeman is an aristocrat.", "attr": "James Henry Hammond"}, "exp_en": "The South's white hierarchy ran from a tiny planter elite to yeomen to a large propertyless class, with racial privilege — \"every freeman is an aristocrat\" — buying the loyalty of those the economy left behind.", "exp_zh": "南方白人的等级从微小的种植园精英到自耕农再到庞大的无产阶层，种族特权——“每个自由人都是贵族”——购买了那些被经济抛弃者的忠诚。", "page": 389, "img": {"file": "img:f1_3087", "credit": "图源：Henretta《America's History》第8版 p.389"}}];